{"id": "a532800a-39d5-468d-b4c5-803b2abb4847", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T00:08:02.823298", "source": "agent", "parent_id": null, "system_prompt": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Collaborate with the researcher to develop an experiment design for the original task. First inspect the masked repository and supplied inputs, then use end_researcher_turn with stage=plan to propose an approach, consequential choices and uncertainties. Wait for explicit researcher approval before developing the full design. After approval, hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer, supported by rationale, controls, feasible checks and repository observations in evidence. State assumptions separately from fixed task requirements. No executed experiment or invented outcome is required for this design-only task. Use inspect_repository and execute_check for exploration. Share concrete findings: private tool output is not automatically sent to the researcher. Revise when needed; do not invent objections or ambiguities to extend the conversation. The researcher decides when to stop."}, "tools": [{"description": "List a repository directory or read a text file. Paths are relative to the task workspace.", "action_type": "InspectRepositoryAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "InspectRepositoryTool", "title": "inspect_repository"}, {"description": "Run a shell command in the isolated task workspace. Use small exploratory checks before submitting your plan.", "action_type": "ExecuteCheckAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ExecuteCheckTool", "title": "execute_check"}, {"description": "Yield a proposed approach (stage=plan) or completed experiment design (stage=result), with evidence, assumptions and uncertainties. The researcher decides when to finish.", "action_type": "ReviewHandoffAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ReviewHandoffTool", "title": "end_researcher_turn"}], "dynamic_context": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<CURRENT_DATETIME>\nThe current date and time is: 2026-10-25T00:07\n</CURRENT_DATETIME>"}, "kind": "SystemPromptEvent"}
{"id": "3c4412a2-eb90-480c-aaab-0ea2a33ddf47", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T00:08:02.825389", "source": "user", "parent_id": "a532800a-39d5-468d-b4c5-803b2abb4847", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Thanks. Before any design work, please do a scoping pass only — do not produce the full experiment design yet.\\n\\n1) Inspection: confirm what is actually available in this environment (/workspace contents, any local code, model weights, datasets, or attack implementations such as AutoDAN/PAIR harnesses). The track note says design-only, so if nothing is present just state that plainly rather than assuming a stack.\\n\\n2) Proposed approach (outline level, not the deliverable): sketch how you would structure a study of combined jailbreak techniques on ASR, specifically:\\n   - the factor set and how each factor is operationalized: attacker strength (e.g. budget/iterations/target-model access), defense strength (e.g. defense tiers such as none / system-prompt hardening / perplexity-or-input filtering / RLHF-baseline vs strengthened alignment), previously-tested-trick exposure (novel vs previously-publicized transformations), and attack style (token-level AutoDAN vs prompt-level PAIR);\\n   - the design type you favor (fully crossed factorial vs fractional/cblocked) and why, given that AutoDAN and PAIR have very different per-query compute profiles;\\n   - the unit of analysis and the ASR denominator/scoring decision (single-judge vs judge ensemble, refusal detection), including how you would keep scoring unbiased w.r.t. attack style;\\n   - the analysis plan for interaction dynamics (e.g. logistic/mixed-effects model with attacker x defense x style interactions, per-dataset stratification, effect sizes and uncertainty), and what \\\"interaction\\\" you would actually be able to identify versus confound.\\n\\n3) Consequential assumptions and uncertainties: list explicitly what you are assuming rather than know — e.g. whether \\\"datasets\\\" means harm-benchmark query sets vs domain splits, which target models and defense tiers are in scope, judge model choice, compute realistic query budget per cell, and how \\\"previously tested tricks\\\" is represented (held-out vs reused attack library). Mark anything not supported by the brief as an assumption.\\n\\nAlso flag any factor you think is not identifiable in the proposed structure, so we can resolve scope before you draft the design.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How do combined jailbreak techniques—involving attacker strength, defense strength, and previously tested tricks—affect the Attack Success Rate (ASR) of LLMs under both token-level (AutoDAN) and prompt-level (PAIR) attacks? What are the interaction dynamics between attacker power and defense robustness across datasets and attack styles?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/97431/11:setup_17\", \"neurips2024/97431/11:setup_18\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
