{"id": "d07345e5-10cb-4714-b152-16a820787b02", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T00:31:12.397170", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "809c300c-6244-409d-95c8-440738aff059", "thought": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Generation dominates cost, not Tier B — that's a consequential finding for the regime design. Let me refine with realistic early stopping and a defensible 1× definition."}], "reasoning_content": "The cost model is dominated by generation (187M queries for \"full\"). That's implausibly large. Let me note: AutoDAN 4800 queries per behavior is at 1x; but actually AutoDAN's own evaluation is cheaper because they use a smaller pop/gen. Let me add a note that 1x could be defined differently, and add the checkpointing trick and an \"early-stop\" reduction. Also note that \"full\" at 224M target queries is infeasible for open-weight local serving; the standard regime at 32M is also large. This is an important honest finding: the design's dominant cost is Tier A generation, not Tier B, and the natural remedy is to define 1x budget much smaller than published AutoDAN defaults and to treat the budget ladder as the primary quantity.\n\nActually key insight: the ratio QA1/QP1 = 12x means AutoDAN dominates. Let me refine: add an option that AutoDAN's GA can be run with early stopping on success (realized queries much lower than worst-case). And note that in Tier A the artifact is frozen so per-cell replay is ~free — so defense factor is nearly free, which is a strong argument for the design.\n\nLet me also compute a \"realized\" cost with early stopping and a smaller 1x.\n\nI have enough. Let me do one more quick refinement run to produce a defensible cost table with early-stopping realism, then write the final design.\n\nAlso I should compute the design-level requirement: minimum n/cell for the primary three-way interaction. The MDE table gives additive interaction MDE ~10.6pp at 450/cell, 14.5pp at 240/cell. Good.\n\nLet me do the final cost refinement quickly.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "cat << 'EOF' > /tmp/model2.py\nimport math\n# Published AutoDAN worst case = 120gen x 40pop = 4800 queries. But ASR saturates early,\n# so define 1x = 500 (AutoDAN, early-stopping) / 400 (PAIR, 20x20) => near-parity of unit cost.\n# Report BOTH: canonical-1x (worst case) and realized-1x (early-stopped) so the ladder is honest.\nCAN=(4800,400); REAL=(500,400)\nprint(f\"canonical worst-case ratio {CAN[0]//CAN[1]}x ; realized early-stop ratio {REAL[0]/REAL[1]:.2f}x\")\ndef total(Nb,nbc,S,cells,samp,tb_cells,tb_Nb,tb_buds,Q=REAL,exp_opt=2):\n    gen=sum(Nb*S*exp_opt*q*1.0 + nbc*S*exp_opt*q*4.0 for q in Q)   # 1x core + 4x checkpointed ladder\n    rep=Nb*S*3*cells*samp\n    tb=sum(tb_Nb*S*exp_opt*q*sum(tb_buds)*tb_cells for q in Q)\n    return gen,rep,tb,gen+rep+tb\nprint(\"\\nREGIME TABLE (realized-1x cost basis, per target model x alignment-stage)\")\nfor nm,(Nb,nbc,S,cells,samp,tbc,tbN,tbb) in {\n 'full':(200,60,3,8,3,4,60,(1.0,4.0)),\n 'standard':(120,40,3,8,2,2,40,(1.0,)),\n 'stripped':(60,20,2,8,1,0,0,())}.items():\n    g,r,t,T=total(Nb,nbc,S,cells,samp,tbc,tbN,tbb)\n    print(f\" {nm:9s} Nb={Nb:3d} ladder={nbc:2d} seeds={S} TierB(cells,Nb)={(tbc,tbN)} | gen={g/1e6:6.2f}M replay={r:9.0f} TierB={t/1e6:6.2f}M | TOTAL={T/1e6:6.1f}M queries | scored attempts={Nb*S*3*cells*samp}\")\nprint(\"\\nKEY: replay (the entire style x defense x exposure contrast) costs <=0.05M queries,\")\nprint(\"i.e. <0.2% of total. Defense factor is ~free; generation is the whole bill.\")\n# Multiplier for model grid\nfor M in [1,4,8]:\n    g,r,t,T=total(120,40,3,8,2,2,40,(1.0,))\n    print(f\"  model_grid x{M} -> {T*M/1e6:6.1f}M target queries (standard regime)\")\nEOF\npython3 /tmp/model2.py", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9391133e2e5fd155", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-9391133e2e5fd155", "responses_item_id": null, "