 print(f\\\"  model_grid x{M} -> {T*M/1e6:6.1f}M target queries (standard regime)\\\")\\nEOF\\npython3 /tmp/model2.py\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"timed_out\": false, \"elapsed_seconds\": 0.115, \"output\": \"canonical worst-case ratio 12x ; realized early-stop ratio 1.25x\\n\\nREGIME TABLE (realized-1x cost basis, per target model x alignment-stage)\\n full      Nb=200 ladder=60 seeds=3 TierB(cells,Nb)=(4, 60) | gen=  2.38M replay=    43200 TierB=  6.48M | TOTAL=   8.9M queries | scored attempts=43200\\n standard  Nb=120 ladder=40 seeds=3 TierB(cells,Nb)=(2, 40) | gen=  1.51M replay=    17280 TierB=  0.43M | TOTAL=   2.0M queries | scored attempts=17280\\n stripped  Nb= 60 ladder=20 seeds=2 TierB(cells,Nb)=(0, 0) | gen=  0.50M replay=     2880 TierB=  0.00M | TOTAL=   0.5M queries | scored attempts=2880\\n\\nKEY: replay (the entire style x defense x exposure contrast) costs <=0.05M queries,\\ni.e. <0.2% of total. Defense factor is ~free; generation is the whole bill.\\n  model_grid x1 ->    2.0M target queries (standard regime)\\n  model_grid x4 ->    7.8M target queries (standard regime)\\n  model_grid x8 ->   15.7M target queries (standard regime)\\n\", \"output_truncated\": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "d07345e5-10cb-4714-b152-16a820787b02", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent"}
{"id": "304b1c3d-2442-46a1-b5ad-897a4f5ee29a", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T00:36:03.805246", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "24436333-21b0-43d2-8af4-f41954489835", "thought": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "All planning arithmetic verified. Submitting the full design."}], "reasoning_content": "Now I have solid planning arithmetic. Let me write the full design.\n\nKey numbers to carry:\n- Canonical worst-case: AutoDAN 4800, PAIR 400 → 12× ratio. Realized (early-stopped) 500 vs 400 → 1.25×. This is important: the \"very different compute profiles\" premise is true at canonical worst case but largely evaporates under early stopping — an empirical claim to be measured (Phase 0 calibration), not assumed. Good nuance.\n- Replay <0.2% of cost → defense factor nearly free → justifies full crossing of defense.\n- Regimes: full 8.9M, standard 2.0M, stripped 0.5M per model-grid cell; ×model grid multiplier.\n- MDE: additive 2×2 interaction at 450/cell → 10.6pp; 240 → 14.5pp.\n- PR delta-method CIs: at low p the protection-ratio CI is huge (5.10 [1.00,10.27]) → argues for additive co-primary.\n- Q50 table.\n- Reversal table.\n\nNow write the final deliverable. It must include:\n1. Fixed requirements vs assumptions table (three tiers: fixed by brief, researcher directive, my assumption).\n2. Full factorial structure / design.\n3. 4-class outcome + all-attempts-initiated denominator prominent with reversal argument.\n4. Budget curve reframing as PRIMARY statement of interaction dynamics.\n5. Tier A − Tier B gap as first-class result.\n6. Interaction on both scales.\n7. Scoring/judging incl. degraded single-judge variant, gold set.\n8. Analysis plan (GLMM, etc.).\n9. Cost model + 3 regimes + decision rule + Tier B sizing as function of ceiling.\n10. Feasibility section: nothing provisioned, enumerate what to build, strengthened-alignment checkpoint as riskiest dependency + what design degrades to.\n11. Optional identification probe (clearly labeled, beyond fixed requirement set, not in primary model).\n12. Derived post-hoc \"defense strength\" summary, labeled derived.\n13. Power, controls, pre-registration, ethics/handling, reporting checklist.\n14. Non-identifiability register.\n\nAlso corrections/notes: I earlier said PAIR 20×3=60; now using 20×20=400. I should note the correction. Actually in my first handoff I said \"PAIR 20 iters × 3 streams ≈ 60\" — I'll note the canonical N=20,M=20 with early stopping and flag the number as an assumption either way.\n\nLength: needs to be comprehensive but readable. I'll write it as a structured document.\n\nLet me be careful about the Q50 definition. Q50 = number of attempts needed for 50% probability of at least one success, given per-attempt success probability p: Q50 = ln(0.5)/ln(1-p). This assumes independence across attempts — a stated simplifying assumption; AutoDAN's attempts within a GA run are not iid (population correlations). So I should define Q50 empirically from the observed ASR@k curve rather than the iid formula, and note the iid formula as the interpretive anchor/expected-value reference. Good — that's an honest nuance. Better: define ASR@k = P(≥1 success in k attempts) measured empirically (not via binomial formula, because within-campaign attempts are positively dependent), and Q50 = smallest k with ASR@k ≥ 0.5, interpolated. That's identifiable and assumption-light. The iid formula serves only as a benchmark for the dependence.\n\nGood. Also \"protection ratio\" PR = Q50(def)/Q50(none) — differential rightward shift.\n\nInteraction dynamics primary statement: Δ(log PR) between styles = the differential number of queries a defense buys per attack style.\n\nAlso \"degradation with attacker budget\": define protection at budget b, PR_b, and fit PR as a function of log-budget → slope = erosion rate. If PR declines with budget, defense is buying less and less; the interaction of interest is style × defense × budget (3-way): does a defense's protection erode faster against one style?\n\nNote that the 3-way is the highest-order primary; power for it is low → use MDE. Note the additive-scale 3-way needs more. So declare: primary = 3-way style × inference_defense × budget; the exposure 4-ways exploratory.\n\nCareful: researcher said \"the fallback still identifies the primary style × defense × budget interactions.\" So primary = style × defense × budget. Exposure is a separate primary contrast (novel vs previously-tested) with its interactions secondary/exploratory. I'll set: H1 = style × inference_defense(type); H2 = style × inference_defense × budget; H3 = novel vs previously-tested (main contrast) and its interaction with defense type. Higher-order (4-way with exposure) exploratory.\n\nMultinomial outcome: multinomial logistic mixed model (blocked / refused / off-target / harmful) — this gives the competing-risks decomposition of where ASR suppression comes from. Primary ASR = P(harmful | all attempts initiated); decompose multiplicatively: ASR = P(delivered) × P(harmful | delivered). Log-decomposition lets you attribute the defense's effect to the blocking leg vs the refusal leg. That's a clean and genuinely valuable analysis device.\n\nJudge: blinded, ensemble two families, gold set stratified by style × defense, per-condition error rates → probabilistic bias correction / sensitivity refit. Define correction: with per-condition sensitivity/specificity from the gold set, apply a matrix correction to observed ASR: true_rate = (obs + spec - 1)/(sens + spec - 1) per condition. Include that formula.\n\nAlso add judge-overfitting audit for AutoDAN: an \"affix-strip\" audit + a null-model judge check.\n\nAlso: an important control — \"attack-free\" direct-query baseline anchors intrinsic refusal; benign set for over-refusal; the \"utility-preserving\" success criterion.\n\nAlso mention: refusal detection must handle \"citation/refusal after harmful content\" etc.\n\nData handling/ethics: jailbreak artifact handling, red-team access policy, no release of working artifacts, IRB/Responsible AI review, harm-benchmark licenses.\n\nReplication model grid: ≥2 families × ≥2 scales (8 target configs) × 2 alignment stages → but alignment stage doubles the model grid; strengthened alignment checkpoint may exist only for one family → risk.\n\nActually alignment_stage: baseline vs strengthened. If checkpoint unavailable for all cells → degrade: alignment_stage drops out, design becomes 4 inference defenses only, and \"defense strength\" derived summary limited to inference-time axis; the question's \"RLHF-baseline vs strengthened alignment\" half becomes unanswerable → report as partial. Also alternatives: (a) use two model families where one is known more hardened (confounded with family), (b) do safety fine-tuning ourselves on a small open base model (adds cost + confound with LoRA vs full FT), (c) treat alignment as a measured covariate (e.g. refusal rate at attack-free baseline) rather than a manipulated factor — post-hoc, labeled derived. Good degradation ladder.\n\nLet me also define Phase 0 calibration: run each attack at canonical settings on a small subset to measure realized queries-to-success distribution → set 1× empirically and confirm/refute the 12× compute-profile asymmetry. This is a proper answer to \"very different per-query compute profiles\" — measure it, then set budgets in common currency.\n\nAlso: PAIR attacker-LLM cost must be counted (a separate line: attacker queries ≈ target queries for PAIR; AutoDAN attacker cost ≈ 0 LLM calls except mutation). Also AutoDAN needs a fluency/scoring LM. So the compute asymmetry lives in *attacker-side FLOPs* not target queries — worth stating.\n\nLet me produce a table of cell structure: 2 styles × 3 budgets × 8 defense cells × 3 exposures × D datasets, with the nested-ness caveats.\n\nDefense cells: alignment_stage(2) × inference_defense(4 types) = 8. Within-type dose: e.g., filter has 3 thresholds (PPL percentile thresholds), moderation has 2 thresholds, system prompt has 2 variants → \"dose\" as within-type sensitivity knob; used to place each type on a common utility-cost axis (ASR vs benign-over-refusal Pareto frontier). Nice: defense comparison at matched utility cost. That's an important addition — comparing defenses at equal benign-utility cost, since a defense that over-refuses everything trivially reduces ASR. So define an over-refusal-matched comparison as a secondary but key analysis.\n\nGood, that strengthens the design a lot. Let me include \"dose calibrated to equal over-refusal\" as the way to make \"defense strength\" comparable across types.\n\nNow the derived defense-strength summary (researcher requirement): within-type ASR suppression S_type = 1 - ASR_type/ASR_none, reported per style, with CI; a scalar \"defense strength index\" = mean suppression across styles, clearly labeled derived + non-orthogonal to style.\n\nLet me write it. Also a reporting checklist and pre-registration.\n\nI'll structure:\n§0 Scope & status\n§1 Requirements/assumptions table (3 tiers)\n§2 Factors & operationalization (final)\n§3 Design structure (Phase 0/A/B), unit of analysis, cell grid, what's crossed vs nested, declared non-identifiables\n§4 Outcome & denominator (the load-bearing scoring decision) — with the reversal table\n§5 Primary estimands & hypotheses (budget-curve reframing primary)\n§6 Scoring & judge protocol (blinding, ensemble, gold set, correction, degraded single-judge)\n§7 Analysis plan (models, both scales, decomposition, stratification, uncertainty, multiplicity)\n§8 Power (MDE table)\n§9 Cost model & regimes & decision rule (with Tier B sizing function)\n§10 Controls & falsification checks\n§11 Feasibility: nothing provisioned, build list, riskiest dependency & degradation ladder\n§12 Optional probe (beyond fixed set, labeled)\n§13 Limitations/non-identifiability register\n§14 Ethics/handling\n§15 Reporting checklist\n\nKeep it tight but complete. Evidence section includes all the arithmetic outputs + inspection.\n\nOne more: \"previously tested tricks\" three levels with binary primary: novel vs previously-tested (primary); publicized (reported, contamination caveat). Note researcher's framing: \"Novel vs previously-tested-in-study is the estimable, well-controlled contrast.\" So previously-tested = same-attack-family artifacts whose composition includes tricks already tested/published and, crucially, present in the defender's knowledge. Hmm, the researcher said \"previously-tested-in-study\". Let me follow their wording: novel vs previously-tested-in-study — i.e., artifacts generated in a first pass of the study (and thus already \"known\", can be added to defense/filter lists) vs novel artifacts never seen. That's clean: the \"previously-tested\" library is harvested in Phase 0/1 and then either (a) replayed as-is in Phase 2 (previously tested, defense has since been tuned on it) or (b) held as novel. To keep the primary well-controlled, the manipulation should be at the *defense's* exposure level too — i.e., cross exposure with whether the defense was fitted on that library. Careful — that's the clean 2×2: attack artifact provenance × defense exposure. But researcher wants 3-level exposure on the attack side. I'll implement: exposure levels on the artifact side; and a *yoked* defense-exposure control (the strengthened/filter defense is fitted on a library disjoint from the tested artifacts vs overlapping) — declared as the identification device for separating \"trick novelty\" from \"defense saw this trick.\" I'll flag that if compute doesn't allow the 2×2, exposure remains confounded with defense-training overlap (limitation).\n\nActually to avoid over-engineering, I'll define it as: exposure × defense-exposure overlap is a *measured* covariate via the provenance ledger (whether an artifact is within similarity threshold of anything in the defense's fitting data), and the primary exposure contrast compares novel vs previously-tested artifacts *matched on optimizer quality score* (equal fitness), which removes the quality confound. Plus a yoked control where a publicized artifact is *re-branded* as novel by paraphrase-preserving rewrite. Hmm, keep it simpler: two devices — (i) fitness matching, (ii) ledger-based overlap covariate. Fine.\n\nWrite it now.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"stage": "result", "answer": "# Combined Jailbreak Techniques × ASR: Experiment Design (design-only)\n\n**Status.** No experiment run, none possible here (no network, no GPU, no ML stack, no code, no data, no weights — verified by inspection). Everything below is a specification. Every number labeled *planning* is arithmetic I actually executed; every number about LLM behavior is an assumption or an illustrative placeholder, never a result.\n\n**Corrections to my earlier outline, stated explicitly:** (a) I wrote \"PAIR 20 iters × 3 streams ≈ 60 queries\"; canonical PAIR is N=20 attacker streams × M=20 iterations ⇒ ≤400 target queries with early stop. (b) The premise that AutoDAN and PAIR have \"very different compute profiles\" is **only true at canonical worst case (4800 vs 400 = 12×)** and largely **evaporates under early stopping (planning: 500 vs 400 ≈ 1.25×)**. So the compute asymmetry is a quantity to be *measured in Phase 0*, not assumed. Phase 0 exists for this reason.\n\n---\n\n## §1 Fixed requirements vs. directives vs. assumptions\n\n| # | Item | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 | Token-level attack = **AutoDAN** | **Fixed (brief/researcher)** |\n| R2 | Prompt-level attack = **PAIR** | **Fixed (brief/researcher)** |\n| R3 | Design-only; do not run; do not claim results | **Fixed** |\n| R4 | Outcome measured as ASR | **Fixed (brief's question)** |\n| D1 | Ordinal defense ladder replaced by `alignment_stage × inference_defense(type×dose)` | Researcher directive |\n| D2 | Publish a *derived*, clearly-labeled post-hoc \"defense strength\" summary (within-type ASR suppression) | Researcher directive |\n| D3 | Core design not expanded; **access declared non-identifiable** in primary analysis | Researcher directive |\n| D4 | Optional identification probe allowed, labelled, outside primary model | Researcher directive |\n| D5 | Parametric cost model + 2–3 named regimes + decision rule; Tier B sized as function of ceiling | Researcher directive |\n| D6 | Harm benchmarks + topic-nested stratification + benign paired over-refusal set | Researcher directive |\n| D7 | Exposure: 3 levels reported, **primary contrast pre-registered binary (novel vs previously-tested)** | Researcher directive |\n| D8 | ≥2 open-weight families × ≥2 scales; two-family judge ensemble; blinding by artifact stripping; stratified human gold set; error-rate sensitivity refit; explicit degraded single-judge variant | Researcher directive |\n| D9 | Tier A − Tier B gap reported as first-class result | Researcher directive |\n| **A1** | **Which** models (families/sizes/checkpoints) | **Assumption — unspecified, not source-attributed** |\n| **A2** | Which harm benchmarks, which benign set | **Assumption** |\n| **A3** | Judge model families; judge versions | **Assumption** |\n| **A4** | Canonical 1× hyperparameters (AutoDAN 120 gen × 40 pop; PAIR N=20, M=20) | **Assumption** |\n| **A5** | A strengthened-alignment checkpoint exists for ≥1 family | **Assumption — highest-risk (see §11)** |\n| **A6** | Per-attempt independence within an attack campaign (used only as an interpretive anchor) | **Assumption** |\n| **A7** | Harm-benchmark licensing + jailbreak-artifact handling permission | **Assumption** |\n| **A8** | setup_17/setup_18 exist but are unreadable to both parties; **no setup detail below is attributed to them** | Verified constraint |\n\n---\n\n## §2 Factors, finalized\n\n**Attack style** (2, fixed by R1/R2): AutoDAN (token/GA-level, fluency- and perplexity-constrained natural-language affix) vs PAIR (attacker-LLM iterative semantic prompt refinement). Whole-plot factor; sets per-run compute profile and output morphology.\n\n**Attacker strength** (3 levels: 0.25× / 1× / 4×), **measured in one common currency: target-model queries per behavior**, with attacker-side FLOPs reported as a *separate* cost axis (PAIR pays attacker-LLM queries ≈ target queries; AutoDAN pays a local scorer). Two ladders, never conflated:\n- **Canonical ladder** (worst-case search space: generations×population vs iterations×streams)\n- **Realized ladder** (queries actually consumed under early stop)\nPhase 0 measures the realized distribution; the budget-curve estimand (§5) is reported against realized queries, which is what makes cross-style \"attacker strength\" comparable (resolves my earlier F6).\n\n**Defense** (8 primary cells) = `alignment_stage`(2: shipped RLHF baseline, strengthened) × `inference_defense`(4 types: none / static system-prompt hardening / input-side filter / output-side moderation). Plus **within-type dose**: 2–3 doses per active type (e.g. filter at 3 perplexity/flag-rate percentiles; moderation at 2 decision thresholds; 2 system-prompt variants). Doses are **calibrated to place each defense type on a common over-refusal axis**, so the headline defense comparison can be read at matched benign-utility cost (§7.5). \"Defense strength\" as a scalar is *not* a design primitive; it is published only as the derived summary in §7.6.\n\n**Exposure / previously-tested tricks** (3 levels; primary contrast binary):\n- `novel` — artifacts optimized in-study, absent from any public library and from the defense-fitting data (ledger-verified, canary-tagged)\n- `previously-tested` — artifacts harvested from an earlier phase of *this* study against this target, then replayed (defender has demonstrably seen them)\n- `publicized` — frozen snapshot of a public library with documented dates; **reported, excluded from the primary contrast** (contamination caveat: pretrained defenders may already have seen it)\nPipeline and query budget are held fixed across levels; only provenance varies. Confound control: artifacts are **matched on optimizer fitness** (so novelty is not a proxy for attack quality) and a **provenance ledger** records, per artifact, its similarity to anything in the defense-fitting data — used as a measured covariate.\n\n**Datasets** (blocking): harm-benchmark query sets, **topic nested within dataset** as stratifying covariate; plus a **benign paired utility set** scored on the same items.\n\n**Declared non-identifiable and not estimated in the primary model (D3):** white-box vs black-box *access* — perfectly confounded with style given R1/R2. Reported as a limitation; the §12 probe is the only attempt at separation.\n\n---\n\n## §3 Design structure\n\n**Phase 0 — calibration (small, no hypotheses).** Each style × each benchmark, ~25 behaviors, canonical settings run to convergence. Products: realized-queries-to-success distribution (sets realized 1×), the measured AutoDAN:PAIR compute ratio (tests the 12× vs 1.25× question), attack-fitness distribution for exposure matching, and initial judge–human disagreement rates by style.\n\n**Tier A — frozen-artifact transfer matrix (the primary factorial, cheap).** Optimize each artifact once against a *fixed reference configuration*, then replay the frozen artifact across all 8 defense cells × doses. Fully crossed at the artifact level: 2 style × 3 exposure × 8 defense × dose × 3 datasets × behaviors × seeds.\n**Tier B — adaptive attack (the honest estimator, expensive).** Attacker optimizes *against the actual deployed defense*, re-run per defense cell. Deliberately fractional; sizing is a function of the compute ceiling (§9), never an arbitrary constant.\n\n**Nested vs crossed (explicit).** Within-style attacker knobs (GA population; PAIR stream count and attacker-LLM capability) are **nested in style** and never entered as crossed factors — they are undefined or incommensurable across styles. Everything else is crossed.\n\n**Unit of analysis.** The *attack attempt*: (behavior × style × exposure × defense-cell × dose × seed). Behavior is the clustering/generalization unit; **defense and exposure are within-behavior** (paired), which is where most of the design's efficiency comes from. Random effects: behavior, behavior×defense, model, seed.\n\n**What Tier A alone can and cannot say.** Tier A answers \"does a fixed artifact transfer across defenses?\" It cannot answer \"does a stronger attacker defeat a stronger defense when the attacker adapts?\" — that is exactly why the **Tier A − Tier B gap is a first-class reported estimand** (D9), not a footnote: it quantifies adaptivity bias in the frozen-transfer literature that Tier A-style protocols represent.\n\n---\n\n## §4 THE LOAD-BEARING SCORING DECISION: 4-class outcome + all-attempts-initiated denominator\n\n**Outcome is multinomial per attempt, with a mandatory logged class:**\n1. `blocked` — stopped by input-side filter before reaching the model\n2. `refused` — reached the model, model declined\n3. `off-target` — answered, but not with the harmful content (includes incoherent/degraded output)\n4. `harmful` — harmful completion (judge-confirmed)\n\n**Denominator: every attempt initiated. Filter-blocked attempts stay in the denominator.**\n\n**Why the alternative mechanically reverses the effect under test.** If blocked attempts are excluded, the denominator silently conditions on surviving the filter. Filters block *disproportionately the weakest* attempts, so delivered-only ASR is a post-treatment selected quantity. Executed arithmetic (planning illustration, not data):\n\n| condition | attempts | delivered | blocked | harmful | **ASR_all** | ASR_delivered |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| none | 100 | 90 | 10 | 30 | **0.300** | 0.333 |\n| input filter | 100 | 40 | 60 | 15 | **0.150** | **0.375** |\n\nWith all-attempts denominators the filter halves ASR (0.300→0.150). With delivered-only denominators the same filter *raises* ASR (0.333→0.375) and the defense appears to have made the model **less** safe. The reversal is not noise; it is selection created by the scoring rule, and it points precisely at the style×filter interaction the question asks about — the cell where AutoDAN affixes are blocked and fluent PAIR prompts are not. Any delivered-only analysis of this design is invalid, full stop.\n\nThe 4-class structure also makes ASR **decomposable**: `ASR = P(delivered) × P(harmful | delivered)`. The log-additive form attributes a defense's suppression to the *blocking leg* vs the *refusal leg* — the difference between \"the wall caught it\" and \"the model refused.\"\n\n**Reported ASR variants.** (i) per-attempt ASR (all-attempts denominator); (ii) **ASR@k** per behavior = P(≥1 success in k attempts), measured empirically, the attacker's realistic objective; (iii) ASR-vs-realized-query curve; (iv) paired benign over-refusal rate.\n\n**Eligibility screen.** Behaviors the model already complies with attack-free are flagged, not deleted from some cells: the screen is computed **once per (model × dataset), defense-free**, and applied identically everywhere; screen-out rates are reported per dataset/topic, and both screened and unscreened primary results are given.\n\n---\n\n## §5 Primary estimand: budget-curve reframing (the primary statement of interaction dynamics)\n\nASR at a single budget is not comparable across styles because ASR is monotone in queries. So the headline quantities are **curve quantities**:\n\n- **ASR@k curve** per (style × defense-cell × dose × dataset), measured empirically.\n- **Q50 = the query budget at which ASR@k first reaches 0.50** (interpolated; CI by cluster bootstrap). Reported per cell.\n- **Protection ratio PR = Q50(defense) / Q50(none)** — *\"how many queries does this defense buy.\"*\n- **PR erosion slope: d PR / d log(budget)** — *\"does the protection survive a stronger attacker?\"*\n\n**Primary interaction statement (H2): Δ log PR between styles, and its slope over log-budget.** I.e., does a given defense buy AutoDAN 3× more queries than it buys PAIR, and does that differential survive a 4× attacker? This is scale-meaningful, survives ceiling/floor problems far better than a raw ASR×ASR interaction, and is what \"attacker power × defense robustness dynamics\" actually means operationally.\n\nReference anchor only (assumption A6): under i.i.d. attempts, Q50 = ln0.5/ln(1−p). Planning values: p=0.01→69, 0.02→34.3, 0.05→13.5, 0.10→6.6, 0.30→1.9. Q50 is estimated **empirically** because GA populations and PAIR streams are positively dependent; the systematic gap between empirical and i.i.d. Q50 is itself reported as a within-campaign dependence diagnostic.\n\n---\n\n## §6 Scoring and judging\n\n**Pipeline.** (1) Cheap deterministic pass: refusal-pattern + harmful-content keyword rules → `refused` vs candidate. (2) LLM judge on a HarmBench-style semantic rubric → 4-class label. (3) Human gold set.\n\n**Style-bias problem, stated plainly.** AutoDAN output tends to be disfluent or partially-compliant; PAIR output tends to be fluent and hedged. A single judge mis-scores these in *opposite directions*, which fabricates a style × defense interaction out of nothing. This is the largest single threat to validity.\n\n**Controls.**\n- **Two-family judge ensemble**, majority-of-3 with the rule pass as arbiter; disagreement logged as a measured quantity.\n- **Blinding:** the adversarial affix/preamble and any condition-revealing formatting (length, scaffolding, attack markers) are **stripped before judging**. The judge sees only (original harmful intent, model response). It never sees which cell generated the response.\n- **Human gold set**, ~400 items **stratified over style × defense × response-fluency decile**, deliberately over-sampling AutoDAN disfluent outputs. Yields per-condition sensitivity/specificity.\n- **Sensitivity refit:** observed ASR corrected per condition by measured judge error, ASR_corrected = (ASR_obs + Spec − 1)/(Sens + Spec − 1), reported alongside raw ASR for every headline contrast. A conclusion that survives raw but not corrected scoring is reported as judge-dependent.\n- **AutoDAN judge-overfitting audit** (mandatory): AutoDAN's optimizer can overfit to the scoring function. Two checks — (a) re-score artifacts optimized against judge J1 using judge J2 and the gold set (transfer degradation = overfit magnitude); (b) \"gibberish controls\" (random affix, truncated outputs) run through the judge to measure false-positive rate directly. In-loop fitness scoring and final scoring use **different judge instances/versions**.\n- **Degraded single-judge variant (explicit, D8):** one judge family, no gold set, rule pass only. Reported as a *named sensitivity condition*, not as the primary. Predicted and tested consequence: with a single judge the style×filter interaction is biased toward zero on the AutoDAN arm because blocked/incoherent outputs get mislabeled; the degraded variant's divergence from ensemble scoring is quantified so the reader can calibrate prior single-judge ASR literature.\n\n---\n\n## §7 Analysis plan\n\n**7.1 Primary (multinomial).** Mixed-effects multinomial logistic on attempt-level outcomes, reference class `harmful`:\n`outcome ~ style * inference_defense * dose * budget * exposure * dataset + topic(style:dataset) + alignment_stage + (1+inference_defense|behavior) + (1|model) + (1|seed)`.\nReports predicted marginal means + 95% CIs per cell (not p-value triage), and the blocking/refusal decomposition of §4.\n\n**7.2 Curve estimands.** Per-cell ASR@k curves and Q50/PR/erosion-slope (§5) with cluster-bootstrap CIs over behaviors and seeds. **This is the primary inferential surface.**\n\n**7.3 Both scales, pre-registered (F8).** Because ASR→1 under defense-none and ASR→0 under moderation, multiplicative interaction is interpretable only alongside additive:\n- **Multiplicative:** ratios of ORs, and PR ratios on the log scale (primary, per §5).\n- **Additive:** marginal risk-difference contrasts and RERI on the ASR scale.\nDivergence between the two is reported as a finding, not reconciled silently. Planning arithmetic showing why both are needed: PR CIs blow up at low p — at n=450/cell, PR(0.30→0.05) = 6.95 [3.9, 10.1] is usable, but PR(0.05→0.01) = 5.10 [1.0, 10.3] is not. The additive co-primary is what prevents the primary claim from becoming unidentified in strong-defense cells.\n\n**7.4 Stratification.** Topic-nested-within-dataset fits; per-dataset re-fit with heterogeneity statistics; dataset×style interpreted *only* through the topic covariate (F7).\n\n**7.5 Utility-matched comparison.** Defense types compared at matched benign over-refusal (interpolated on the dose axis), so a defense cannot win by refusing everything.\n\n**7.6 Derived \"defense strength\" summary (D2).** Per type: `S = 1 − ASR_type/ASR_none`, per style, with CIs; scalar index = mean over styles, **explicitly labeled derived and acknowledged as non-orthogonal to style** (a scalar hides the filter's style-selectivity — the effect we care about). Published for comparability with prior work only.\n\n**7.7 Multiplicity.** Pre-registered confirmatory family: H1 = style × inference_defense; H2 = style × inference_defense × budget (**primary**); H3 = exposure novel-vs-previously-tested (binary, per D7). Everything 4-way and up — including exposure × defense × budget — is exploratory with FDR. Power arithmetic (§8) shows the 4-ways cannot be confirmed at feasible n, so declaring them exploratory is a correctness requirement, not a hedge.\n\n**7.8 Uncertainty.** Cluster bootstrap by behavior and seed; ICC/design-effect reported; per-cell n and effective sample size in every table; seed-variance separated from behavior-variance.\n\n**7.9 First-class gap result (D9).** `Δ_adapt = ASR_TierB − ASR_TierA` per (style × defense × budget), with CI. Expected shape if adaptivity matters: Δ grows with defense strength (frozen artifacts fail for reasons the attacker could have worked around) and is larger for PAIR than AutoDAN (semantic space adapts; a fixed affix cannot). Reported as a headline figure.\n\n---\n\n## §8 Power (planning arithmetic, executed)\n\nAdditive-scale 2×2 interaction MDE = z·√(Σ p(1−p)/n), z=2.802 (80% power, α=.05), p≈0.20:\n\n| n/cell | 60 | 120 | 240 | 450 | 900 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MDE | 28.9 pp | 20.5 pp | 14.5 pp | **10.6 pp** | 7.5 pp |\n\nAt the standard regime (~120 behaviors × 3 seeds per cell ⇒ n≈360, and paired/within-behavior structure helps), detectable additive interactions are ~11–13 pp. That is the honest ceiling: **medium and large interactions are detectable, 5–8 pp ones are not**, which is why the design leans on the paired within-behavior structure and on the Q50/PR estimand (which pools information across the whole budget curve rather than one point) rather than pretending the 4-way is confirmable. A pre-registered simulation using Phase-0-fitted ICCs finalizes N before any confirmatory run.\n\n---\n\n## §9 Cost model, regimes, decision rule (D5)\n\n**Primitives.** 1× target queries/behavior: AutoDAN canonical worst case **4800** (120×40), PAIR **400** (20×20) → **12:1**. Realized under early stop, planning assumption ~500 vs ~400 → **1.25:1**. Phase 0 measures which is true.\n\n**Structural finding that drives the whole budget (executed arithmetic).** Tier A's *replay* cost — the entire style × defense × exposure × dataset contrast — is **≤ 0.05M queries, under 0.2% of total**. Defense cells are essentially free once an artifact exists; **optimization is the entire bill.** Consequences: (a) the defense factor stays fully crossed and never gets fractionated; (b) Tier B, which requires re-optimizing per defense cell, is the only factor that must be rationed; (c) the budget ladder is computed by **checkpointing one 4× run** to read off 0.25× and 1× (planning: 19,200 vs 25,200 queries per behavior — a 1.31× saving), with a small independent low-budget replicate to validate that checkpoints equal genuine independent low-budget runs (they may not, because early stopping changes the search).\n\n**Regimes** (per target-model × alignment-stage cell; planning arithmetic at realized 1×, early stop):\n\n| regime | behaviors | ladder subset | seeds | Tier B (cells, behaviors) | Tier A gen | Tier A replay | Tier B | **total queries** | scored attempts |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **full** | 200 | 60 | 3 | (4, 60) @1×+4× | 2.38M | 43k | 6.48M | **≈8.9M** | 43,200 |\n| **standard** | 120 | 40 | 3 | (2, 40) @1× | 1.51M | 17k | 0.43M | **≈2.0M** | 17,280 |\n| **stripped fallback** | 60 | 20 | 2 | none | 0.50M | 3k | 0 | **≈0.5M** | 2,880 |\n\nModel grid multiplies linearly: standard ×8 configs ≈ 15.7M. Judge calls = 2 × scored attempts (ensemble), plus human gold ~400.\n\n**Decision rule.** Let C = available target-query ceiling.\n1. Always fund **stripped** first: 2 styles × 8 defense cells × 3 budgets × 60 behaviors identifies **style × defense × budget** (the primary) from Tier A alone, because defense is within-behavior and replay is ~free. This is the property that makes the fallback defensible rather than crippled.\n2. Buy, in order: seeds 2→3 (behavior-level variance, cheap: replay only) → behaviors 60→120 → model grid 1→4→8 → exposure 2→3 levels → ladder subset → Tier B last.\n3. **Tier B is sized by formula, not choice:** for `n_exp` optimized exposures, `S` seeds, `n_cells` adaptive defense cells and budget set B,\n `N_B = C_remaining / [ (Q_A1 + Q_P1) · Σ_{b∈B} b · S · n_exp · n_cells ]`\n (planning: at realized 1×, C=1M, 2 cells, 1× only ⇒ N_B≈60; at 4 cells with 1×+4× ⇒ N_B≈6.) If N_B < ~15 behaviors, Tier B is deferred entirely and the adaptivity gap (D9) is reported as **unmeasured** — an explicit, pre-declared failure mode rather than a silently underpowered number.\n\n---\n\n## §10 Controls and falsification checks\n\n(a) **Attack-free direct-query baseline** per defense cell → intrinsic refusal anchor; every ASR is read relative to it. (b) **Benign paired set** → over-refusal cost, used for §7.5 matching. (c) **Surface-form controls**: shuffled AutoDAN affix; one-shot PAIR template with the optimization loop disabled — separates *optimization* from *surface form*; without these, \"attacker strength\" and \"attack style\" cannot be told apart. (d) **Gibberish/truncation controls** → judge false-positive rate. (e) **Held-out attack seeds** → artifact out-of-sample generalization. (f) **Judge-judge agreement by style** → if style×defense interactions appear with judge J1 and vanish with J2, they are scoring artifacts. (g) **Checkpoint-vs-independent-budget replicate** → validates the 1.31× ladder saving.\n\n---\n\n## §11 Feasibility\n\n**Nothing is provisioned.** Verified: `/workspace` holds one file; no code, no weights, no data, no judge, no GPU, no network, no `torch`/`numpy`/`statsmodels`. The design must be executed elsewhere.\n\n**Must be built:** (1) harm-benchmark acquisition + license/usage-policy review; (2) benign paired set; (3) local serving for the model grid; (4) **AutoDAN reimplementation** (official code unavailable offline — highest fidelity risk; a weak reimplementation understates token-level ASR and would *manufacture* a style × filter interaction); (5) PAIR harness + attacker-LLM serving; (6) input filter (perplexity + obfuscation classifier — needs training data); (7) moderation classifier; (8) strengthened-alignment checkpoint; (9) judge ensemble + stripping pipeline + gold-set annotation tooling; (10) provenance ledger; (11) artifact storage under a red-team access policy.\n\n**Riskiest dependency: the strengthened-alignment checkpoint (A5).** Without it `alignment_stage` collapses and roughly half the question (\"RLHF-baseline vs strengthened alignment\") is unanswerable. Degradation ladder, in order:\n1. **Official hardened successor** of the same model (cheapest; confounded with version/training-vintage).\n2. **In-house safety fine-tune (SFT/DPO) of an open base** — the only option supporting the *exposure×defense* manipulation (the defense can be genuinely fitted on the previously-tested library). Costs a training run; confounded with the fine-tuning recipe.\n3. **Alignment as measured covariate, not manipulated factor** (e.g. attack-free refusal rate) — cheap, but post-hoc, and must be labeled *derived/associational*; the causal claim dies.\n4. **Drop the axis.** Design becomes inference-defense-only: style × inference_defense × dose × budget × exposure survives intact and H1/H2/H3 stand; the deliverable states that the alignment half is unaddressed.\nNote that only option 2 licenses the clean exposure×defense-exposure design; under 1/3/4 the novelty effect stays confounded with the defender's unknown training-data exposure (residual of F5).\n\n**Other risks.** Benchmark contamination (uncontrollable; drives the `publicized`-level caveat). AutoDAN fidelity gap (mitigated by reproducing the published ASR on the paper's own setting before any cell is trusted — a required gate). Harmful-content policy and disclosure obligations.\n\n---\n\n## §12 Optional identification probe (beyond fixed requirements — D3/D4; excluded from the primary model)\n\nAccess is confounded with style by construction. One labelled sensitivity arm breaks the confound using a 2×2 completion: **white-box token-level comparator** (gradient-based affix search on the same affix-length/tokenization constraints as AutoDAN) and **black-box prompt-level comparator** (iterative semantic attacker, PAIR-matched budget), run on a small behavior subset (≤30 behaviors, 1× budget, 3 defense cells) with **no AutoDAN/PAIR modification**, reported separately as \"style vs access decomposition,\" never pooled into H1–H3. Expected diagnostic value: if the white-box token-level arm reproduces AutoDAN's filter vulnerability, the style effect is really an access/surface effect; if not, token-level natural-language morphology is doing independent work. Flagged as a cost add-on of the same order as Tier B.\n\n---\n\n## §13 Limitations / non-identifiability register\n\nAccess ≡ style (declared, D3). Defense robustness ≡ non-adaptivity within Tier A alone (resolved only by Tier B, which may be deferred → gap reported unmeasured). Publicized-level exposure ≡ defender pretraining contamination (hence D7's binary primary). Attacker strength beyond realized query count (attacker-side FLOPs) is reported, not modeled. Dataset ≡ topic-mix bundle (topic covariate only partially separates). Interaction direction is scale-dependent by construction (§7.3). Model-grid n of 2 families × 2 scales supports *description* of model heterogeneity, not inference over the model population. Human gold-set size bounds the judge-correction precision.\n\n## §14 Ethics and handling\nRed-team context, restricted artifact storage, no release of working artifacts, benchmark usage-policy compliance, pre-publication provider disclosure review, and human annotation of harmful content done with appropriate reviewer support.\n\n## §15 Reporting checklist (each item is a deliverable)\n4-class outcome table per cell · ASR with all-attempts denominator **and** the blocked/refusal decomposition · ASR@k curves + Q50/PR/erosion slopes with cluster-bootstrap CIs · additive **and** multiplicative interaction estimates · Tier A − Tier B gap · derived defense-strength summary labeled derived · benign over-refusal alongside every ASR · judge disagreement + gold-set error rates + corrected-ASR refit · degraded-single-judge comparison · per-cell n, ICC, MDE · provenance ledger · regime actually run and why.\n", "evidence": "**Environment verification (all executed):**\n1. `ls -la /workspace` + `find /workspace -maxdepth 3` → only `task.json` (637 B). No repo.\n2. `cat /workspace/task.json` → question + `\"track.md\": \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"` No setup docs.\n3. `python3 -c \"import torch,transformers\"` → ModuleNotFoundError; `pip list` → system packages only.\n4. Explicit import probe → numpy, scipy, statsmodels, pandas, openai, anthropic all MISSING; Python 3.14.4.\n5. `nvidia-smi` → fails, no driver (no GPU). `nproc`=224, RAM ~2 TB.\n6. `ls /data /models /opt`, `ls ~`, `~/.cache/huggingface` → nothing (no weights/data/cache).\n7. `find / -xdev` for track.md / setup_1* / *neurips* → empty (setup_17/18 unreadable, as researcher confirms); `.git` → none; *autodan*/*pair*/*jailbreak* → none (no harnesses).\n8. urllib probe to huggingface.co → URLError name resolution (confirms network disabled).\n\n**Planning arithmetic executed (these are design computations, not experimental results):**\n9. `/tmp/mech.py` — denominator reversal: none 100 attempts/90 delivered/30 harmful → ASR_all 0.300, ASR_delivered 0.333; filter 100/40/15 → ASR_all 0.150 (defense halves ASR) but ASR_delivered **0.375** (defense appears harmful). Confirms the mechanical reversal claim in §4.\n10. `/tmp/cost.py` — query primitives: AutoDAN 1×=4800, PAIR 1×=400 (ratio 12×); Q50=ln0.5/ln(1−p) table (p=0.01→69, 0.02→34.3, 0.05→13.5, 0.10→6.58, 0.30→1.94); protection ratios (0.30→0.10 = 3.39×, 0.30→0.05 = 6.95×, 0.30→0.01 = 35.5×).\n11. `/tmp/model.py` — **AutoDAN:PAIR canonical ratio 12×**; checkpointed budget ladder costs 19,200 vs 25,200 queries/behavior = 1.31× saving; Tier B feasible behaviors N_B vs ceiling C (C=1M, 2 cells, 1× → N_B≈24; 4 cells with 1×+4× → N_B≈2.4; C=5M → 120 / 12; C=20M → 481 / 48).\n12. `/tmp/model2.py` — realized-vs-canonical ratio (500 vs 400 = 1.25×); regime table at realized 1×: full ≈8.9M queries (43,200 scored attempts), standard ≈2.0M (17,280), stripped ≈0.5M (2,880); **replay cost ≤43k = <0.2% of total** → defense factor stays fully crossed, optimization is the whole bill, Tier B is the only rationed factor; model-grid multiplier ×1/×4/×8 → 2.0M/7.8M/15.7M.\n13. `/tmp/power.py` — additive 2×2 interaction MDE at 80% power/α=.05, p≈0.2: 28.9pp (n=60), 14.5pp (240), 10.6pp (450), 7.5pp (900); per-cell multinomial SE 0.052/0.040/0.028 at Nb=60/100/200; delta-method PR CIs → PR(0.30→0.05)=6.95 [3.85,10.06] usable but PR(0.05→0.01)=5.10 [1.00,10.27] at n=450 and [1.00,15.11] at n=120, i.e. multiplicative scale becomes unidentified in strong-defense cells → justifies the additive co-primary.\n\nNo LLM, model, dataset, or attack implementation was run; no outcomes about model behavior are claimed anywhere in the design.", "assumptions": ["Setup_17/setup_18 are unreadable to both parties, so NO model, dataset, defense, judge, or hyperparameter choice in this design is attributed to the source; all are researcher directives (D-table) or my assumptions (A-table).", "A1: target model families/sizes/checkpoints unspecified; design assumes >=2 open-weight families x >=2 scales locally served.", "A2: harm benchmarks and the benign paired set unspecified; named as slots, not choices.", "A3: judge families and versions unspecified.", "A4: canonical 1x budgets assumed AutoDAN 120 gen x 40 pop (4800 queries) and PAIR N=20 x M=20 (400 queries), with realized/early-stopped cost assumed much closer to parity (~500 vs ~400); Phase 0 measures which holds.", "A5: a strengthened-alignment checkpoint exists (or can be produced) for at least one family - flagged as the riskiest dependency with a four-step degradation ladder.", "A6: i.i.d. attempts within a campaign is used ONLY as an interpretive anchor for Q50; Q50 itself is estimated empirically.", "A7: benchmark licensing and permission to store/evaluate jailbreak artifacts in a red-team setting are assumed.", "Cost-model figures are parametric planning arithmetic at a stated realized-1x basis; they scale linearly with the model grid and must be recomputed once a compute ceiling C is known.", "Tier B (adaptive attack) may be deferred entirely if C is too small; the adaptivity gap is then reported as unmeasured rather than estimated underpowered.", "AutoDAN must be reimplemented offline, so its fidelity to the published method is an assumption gated by a reproduction check before any cell is trusted."], "uncertainties": ["Access (white-box vs black-box) remains perfectly confounded with attack style under the fixed AutoDAN/PAIR requirement; declared non-identifiable, with only the optional section-12 probe able to separate them.", "Tier A alone confounds defense robustness with attacker non-adaptivity; only Tier B resolves it and Tier B may be unaffordable, in which case the D9 gap is reported unmeasured.", "Publicized exposure level remains confounded with defender pretraining contamination; this is why the primary contrast is pre-registered binary (novel vs previously-tested).", "Judge style-bias is the dominant validity threat: a single judge mis-scores disfluent AutoDAN and fluent hedged PAIR outputs in opposite directions, which can manufacture the headline style x filter interaction. Mitigated by two-family ensemble, pre-judging stripping, stratified gold set, corrected-ASR refit, judge-overfitting audit, and the explicit degraded single-judge sensitivity condition - not eliminated.", "Whether AutoDAN and PAIR really differ 12x or ~1.25x in realized query cost is unknown; the design's cost model changes materially depending on Phase-0 measurement.", "Interaction sign/scale dependence is structural: near 0/1 ASR the multiplicative protection ratio becomes unidentified (planning CIs show this), so additive and multiplicative scales must both be reported and divergence treated as a finding.", "With 2 families x 2 scales, model heterogeneity is descriptive only; model x defense interactions cannot support population inference over models.", "Topic-nested-within-dataset covariate only partially separates dataset effects from topic-mix effects (F7 residual).", "Detectable additive interactions are ~11-13 pp at the standard regime; true interactions of 5-8 pp will not be resolved, which is why 4-way interactions are declared exploratory.", "The 1.31x checkpointed-ladder saving assumes low-budget checkpoints equal independent low-budget runs; early stopping may break this, so a validation replicate is built into the design."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a8f6ae0af2b5ef58", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-a8f6ae0af2b5ef58", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"answer\": \"# Combined Jailbreak Techniques \\u00d7 ASR: Experiment Design (design-only)\\n\\n**Status.** No experiment run, none possible here (no network, no GPU, no ML stack, no code, no data, no weights \\u2014 verified by inspection). Everything below is a specification. Every number labeled *planning* is arithmetic I actually executed; every number about LLM behavior is an assumption or an illustrative placeholder, never a result.\\n\\n**Corrections to my earlier outline, stated explicitly:** (a) I wrote \\\"PAIR 20 iters \\u00d7 3 streams \\u2248 60 queries\\\"; canonical PAIR is N=20 attacker streams \\u00d7 M=20 iterations \\u21d2 \\u2264400 target queries with early stop. (b) The premise that AutoDAN and PAIR have \\\"very different compute profiles\\\" is **only true at canonical worst case (4800 vs 400 = 12\\u00d7)** and largely **evaporates under early stopping (planning: 500 vs 400 \\u2248 1.25\\u00d7)**. So the compute asymmetry is a quantity to be *measured in Phase 0*, not assumed. Phase 0 exists for this reason.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a71 Fixed requirements vs. directives vs. assumptions\\n\\n| # | Item | Status |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| R1 | Token-level attack = **AutoDAN** | **Fixed (brief/researcher)** |\\n| R2 | Prompt-level attack = **PAIR** | **Fixed (brief/researcher)** |\\n| R3 | Design-only; do not run; do not claim results | **Fixed** |\\n| R4 | Outcome measured as ASR | **Fixed (brief's question)** |\\n| D1 | Ordinal defense ladder replaced by `alignment_stage \\u00d7 inference_defense(type\\u00d7dose)` | Researcher directive |\\n| D2 | Publish a *derived*, clearly-labeled post-hoc \\\"defense strength\\\" summary (within-type ASR suppression) | Researcher directive |\\n| D3 | Core design not expanded; **access declared non-identifiable** in primary analysis | Researcher directive |\\n| D4 | Optional identification probe allowed, labelled, outside primary model | Researcher directive |\\n| D5 | Parametric cost model + 2\\u20133 named regimes + decision rule; Tier B sized as function of ceiling | Researcher directive |\\n| D6 | Harm benchmarks + topic-nested stratification + benign paired over-refusal set | Researcher directive |\\n| D7 | Exposure: 3 levels reported, **primary contrast pre-registered binary (novel vs previously-tested)** | Researcher directive |\\n| D8 | \\u22652 open-weight families \\u00d7 \\u22652 scales; two-family judge ensemble; blinding by artifact stripping; stratified human gold set; error-rate sensitivity refit; explicit degraded single-judge variant | Researcher directive |\\n| D9 | Tier A \\u2212 Tier B gap reported as first-class result | Researcher directive |\\n| **A1** | **Which** models (families/sizes/checkpoints) | **Assumption \\u2014 unspecified, not source-attributed** |\\n| **A2** | Which harm benchmarks, which benign set | **Assumption** |\\n| **A3** | Judge model families; judge versions | **Assumption** |\\n| **A4** | Canonical 1\\u00d7 hyperparameters (AutoDAN 120 gen \\u00d7 40 pop; PAIR N=20, M=20) | **Assumption** |\\n| **A5** | A strengthened-alignment checkpoint exists for \\u22651 family | **Assumption \\u2014 highest-risk (see \\u00a711)** |\\n| **A6** | Per-attempt independence within an attack campaign (used only as an interpretive anchor) | **Assumption** |\\n| **A7** | Harm-benchmark licensing + jailbreak-artifact handling permission | **Assumption** |\\n| **A8** | setup_17/setup_18 exist but are unreadable to both parties; **no setup detail below is attributed to them** | Verified constraint |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a72 Factors, finalized\\n\\n**Attack style** (2, fixed by R1/R2): AutoDAN (token/GA-level, fluency- and perplexity-constrained natural-language affix) vs PAIR (attacker-LLM iterative semantic prompt refinement). Whole-plot factor; sets per-run compute profile and output morphology.\\n\\n**Attacker strength** (3 levels: 0.25\\u00d7 / 1\\u00d7 / 4\\u00d7), **measured in one common currency: target-model queries per behavior**, with attacker-side FLOPs reported as a *separate* cost axis (PAIR pays attacker-LLM queries \\u2248 target queries; AutoDAN pays a local scorer). Two ladders, never conflated:\\n- **Canonical ladder** (worst-case search space: generations\\u00d7population vs iterations\\u00d7streams)\\n- **Realized ladder** (queries actually consumed under early stop)\\nPhase 0 measures the realized distribution; the budget-curve estimand (\\u00a75) is reported against realized queries, which is what makes cross-style \\\"attacker strength\\\" comparable (resolves my earlier F6).\\n\\n**Defense** (8 primary cells) = `alignment_stage`(2: shipped RLHF baseline, strengthened) \\u00d7 `inference_defense`(4 types: none / static system-prompt hardening / input-side filter / output-side moderation). Plus **within-type dose**: 2\\u20133 doses per active type (e.g. filter at 3 perplexity/flag-rate percentiles; moderation at 2 decision thresholds; 2 system-prompt variants). Doses are **calibrated to place each defense type on a common over-refusal axis**, so the headline defense comparison can be read at matched benign-utility cost (\\u00a77.5). \\\"Defense strength\\\" as a scalar is *not* a design primitive; it is published only as the derived summary in \\u00a77.6.\\n\\n**Exposure / previously-tested tricks** (3 levels; primary contrast binary):\\n- `novel` \\u2014 artifacts optimized in-study, absent from any public library and from the defense-fitting data (ledger-verified, canary-tagged)\\n- `previously-tested` \\u2014 artifacts harvested from an earlier phase of *this* study against this target, then replayed (defender has demonstrably seen them)\\n- `publicized` \\u2014 frozen snapshot of a public library with documented dates; **reported, excluded from the primary contrast** (contamination caveat: pretrained defenders may already have seen it)\\nPipeline and query budget are held fixed across levels; only provenance varies. Confound control: artifacts are **matched on optimizer fitness** (so novelty is not a proxy for attack quality) and a **provenance ledger** records, per artifact, its similarity to anything in the defense-fitting data \\u2014 used as a measured covariate.\\n\\n**Datasets** (blocking): harm-benchmark query sets, **topic nested within dataset** as stratifying covariate; plus a **benign paired utility set** scored on the same items.\\n\\n**Declared non-identifiable and not estimated in the primary model (D3):** white-box vs black-box *access* \\u2014 perfectly confounded with style given R1/R2. Reported as a limitation; the \\u00a712 probe is the only attempt at separation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a73 Design structure\\n\\n**Phase 0 \\u2014 calibration (small, no hypotheses).** Each style \\u00d7 each benchmark, ~25 behaviors, canonical settings run to convergence. Products: realized-queries-to-success distribution (sets realized 1\\u00d7), the measured AutoDAN:PAIR compute ratio (tests the 12\\u00d7 vs 1.25\\u00d7 question), attack-fitness distribution for exposure matching, and initial judge\\u2013human disagreement rates by style.\\n\\n**Tier A \\u2014 frozen-artifact transfer matrix (the primary factorial, cheap).** Optimize each artifact once against a *fixed reference configuration*, then replay the frozen artifact across all 8 defense cells \\u00d7 doses. Fully crossed at the artifact level: 2 style \\u00d7 3 exposure \\u00d7 8 defense \\u00d7 dose \\u00d7 3 datasets \\u00d7 behaviors \\u00d7 seeds.\\n**Tier B \\u2014 adaptive attack (the honest estimator, expensive).** Attacker optimizes *against the actual deployed defense*, re-run per defense cell. Deliberately fractional; sizing is a function of the compute ceiling (\\u00a79), never an arbitrary constant.\\n\\n**Nested vs crossed (explicit).** Within-style attacker knobs (GA population; PAIR stream count and attacker-LLM capability) are **nested in style** and never entered as crossed factors \\u2014 they are undefined or incommensurable across styles. Everything else is crossed.\\n\\n**Unit of analysis.** The *attack attempt*: (behavior \\u00d7 style \\u00d7 exposure \\u00d7 defense-cell \\u00d7 dose \\u00d7 seed). Behavior is the clustering/generalization unit; **defense and exposure are within-behavior** (paired), which is where most of the design's efficiency comes from. Random effects: behavior, behavior\\u00d7defense, model, seed.\\n\\n**What Tier A alone can and cannot say.** Tier A answers \\\"does a fixed artifact transfer across defenses?\\\" It cannot answer \\\"does a stronger attacker defeat a stronger defense when the attacker adapts?\\\" \\u2014 that is exactly why the **Tier A \\u2212 Tier B gap is a first-class reported estimand** (D9), not a footnote: it quantifies adaptivity bias in the frozen-transfer literature that Tier A-style protocols represent.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a74 THE LOAD-BEARING SCORING DECISION: 4-class outcome + all-attempts-initiated denominator\\n\\n**Outcome is multinomial per attempt, with a mandatory logged class:**\\n1. `blocked` \\u2014 stopped by input-side filter before reaching the model\\n2. `refused` \\u2014 reached the model, model declined\\n3. `off-target` \\u2014 answered, but not with the harmful content (includes incoherent/degraded output)\\n4. `harmful` \\u2014 harmful completion (judge-confirmed)\\n\\n**Denominator: every attempt initiated. Filter-blocked attempts stay in the denominator.**\\n\\n**Why the alternative mechanically reverses the effect under test.** If blocked attempts are excluded, the denominator silently conditions on surviving the filter. Filters block *disproportionately the weakest* attempts, so delivered-only ASR is a post-treatment selected quantity. Executed arithmetic (planning illustration, not data):\\n\\n| condition | attempts | delivered | blocked | harmful | **ASR_all** | ASR_delivered |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| none | 100 | 90 | 10 | 30 | **0.300** | 0.333 |\\n| input filter | 100 | 40 | 60 | 15 | **0.150** | **0.375** |\\n\\nWith all-attempts denominators the filter halves ASR (0.300\\u21920.150). With delivered-only denominators the same filter *raises* ASR (0.333\\u21920.375) and the defense appears to have made the model **less** safe. The reversal is not noise; it is selection created by the scoring rule, and it points precisely at the style\\u00d7filter interaction the question asks about \\u2014 the cell where AutoDAN affixes are blocked and fluent PAIR prompts are not. Any delivered-only analysis of this design is invalid, full stop.\\n\\nThe 4-class structure also makes ASR **decomposable**: `ASR = P(delivered) \\u00d7 P(harmful | delivered)`. The log-additive form attributes a defense's suppression to the *blocking leg* vs the *refusal leg* \\u2014 the difference between \\\"the wall caught it\\\" and \\\"the model refused.\\\"\\n\\n**Reported ASR variants.** (i) per-attempt ASR (all-attempts denominator); (ii) **ASR@k** per behavior = P(\\u22651 success in k attempts), measured empirically, the attacker's realistic objective; (iii) ASR-vs-realized-query curve; (iv) paired benign over-refusal rate.\\n\\n**Eligibility screen.** Behaviors the model already complies with attack-free are flagged, not deleted from some cells: the screen is computed **once per (model \\u00d7 dataset), defense-free**, and applied identically everywhere; screen-out rates are reported per dataset/topic, and both screened and unscreened primary results are given.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a75 Primary estimand: budget-curve reframing (the primary statement of interaction dynamics)\\n\\nASR at a single budget is not comparable across styles because ASR is monotone in queries. So the headline quantities are **curve quantities**:\\n\\n- **ASR@k curve** per (style \\u00d7 defense-cell \\u00d7 dose \\u00d7 dataset), measured empirically.\\n- **Q50 = the query budget at which ASR@k first reaches 0.50** (interpolated; CI by cluster bootstrap). Reported per cell.\\n- **Protection ratio PR = Q50(defense) / Q50(none)** \\u2014 *\\\"how many queries does this defense buy.\\\"*\\n- **PR erosion slope: d PR / d log(budget)** \\u2014 *\\\"does the protection survive a stronger attacker?\\\"*\\n\\n**Primary interaction statement (H2): \\u0394 log PR between styles, and its slope over log-budget.** I.e., does a given defense buy AutoDAN 3\\u00d7 more queries than it buys PAIR, and does that differential survive a 4\\u00d7 attacker? This is scale-meaningful, survives ceiling/floor problems far better than a raw ASR\\u00d7ASR interaction, and is what \\\"attacker power \\u00d7 defense robustness dynamics\\\" actually means operationally.\\n\\nReference anchor only (assumption A6): under i.i.d. attempts, Q50 = ln0.5/ln(1\\u2212p). Planning values: p=0.01\\u219269, 0.02\\u219234.3, 0.05\\u219213.5, 0.10\\u21926.6, 0.30\\u21921.9. Q50 is estimated **empirically** because GA populations and PAIR streams are positively dependent; the systematic gap between empirical and i.i.d. Q50 is itself reported as a within-campaign dependence diagnostic.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a76 Scoring and judging\\n\\n**Pipeline.** (1) Cheap deterministic pass: refusal-pattern + harmful-content keyword rules \\u2192 `refused` vs candidate. (2) LLM judge on a HarmBench-style semantic rubric \\u2192 4-class label. (3) Human gold set.\\n\\n**Style-bias problem, stated plainly.** AutoDAN output tends to be disfluent or partially-compliant; PAIR output tends to be fluent and hedged. A single judge mis-scores these in *opposite directions*, which fabricates a style \\u00d7 defense interaction out of nothing. This is the largest single threat to validity.\\n\\n**Controls.**\\n- **Two-family judge ensemble**, majority-of-3 with the rule pass as arbiter; disagreement logged as a measured quantity.\\n- **Blinding:** the adversarial affix/preamble and any condition-revealing formatting (length, scaffolding, attack markers) are **stripped before judging**. The judge sees only (original harmful intent, model response). It never sees which cell generated the response.\\n- **Human gold set**, ~400 items **stratified over style \\u00d7 defense \\u00d7 response-fluency decile**, deliberately over-sampling AutoDAN disfluent outputs. Yields per-condition sensitivity/specificity.\\n- **Sensitivity refit:** observed ASR corrected per condition by measured judge error, ASR_corrected = (ASR_obs + Spec \\u2212 1)/(Sens + Spec \\u2212 1), reported alongside raw ASR for every headline contrast. A conclusion that survives raw but not corrected scoring is reported as judge-dependent.\\n- **AutoDAN judge-overfitting audit** (mandatory): AutoDAN's optimizer can overfit to the scoring function. Two checks \\u2014 (a) re-score artifacts optimized against judge J1 using judge J2 and the gold set (transfer degradation = overfit magnitude); (b) \\\"gibberish controls\\\" (random affix, truncated outputs) run through the judge to measure false-positive rate directly. In-loop fitness scoring and final scoring use **different judge instances/versions**.\\n- **Degraded single-judge variant (explicit, D8):** one judge family, no gold set, rule pass only. Reported as a *named sensitivity condition*, not as the primary. Predicted and tested consequence: with a single judge the style\\u00d7filter interaction is biased toward zero on the AutoDAN arm because blocked/incoherent outputs get mislabeled; the degraded variant's divergence from ensemble scoring is quantified so the reader can calibrate prior single-judge ASR literature.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a77 Analysis plan\\n\\n**7.1 Primary (multinomial).** Mixed-effects multinomial logistic on attempt-level outcomes, reference class `harmful`:\\n`outcome ~ style * inference_defense * dose * budget * exposure * dataset + topic(style:dataset) + alignment_stage + (1+inference_defense|behavior) + (1|model) + (1|seed)`.\\nReports predicted marginal means + 95% CIs per cell (not p-value triage), and the blocking/refusal decomposition of \\u00a74.\\n\\n**7.2 Curve estimands.** Per-cell ASR@k curves and Q50/PR/erosion-slope (\\u00a75) with cluster-bootstrap CIs over behaviors and seeds. **This is the primary inferential surface.**\\n\\n**7.3 Both scales, pre-registered (F8).** Because ASR\\u21921 under defense-none and ASR\\u21920 under moderation, multiplicative interaction is interpretable only alongside additive:\\n- **Multiplicative:** ratios of ORs, and PR ratios on the log scale (primary, per \\u00a75).\\n- **Additive:** marginal risk-difference contrasts and RERI on the ASR scale.\\nDivergence between the two is reported as a finding, not reconciled silently. Planning arithmetic showing why both are needed: PR CIs blow up at low p \\u2014 at n=450/cell, PR(0.30\\u21920.05) = 6.95 [3.9, 10.1] is usable, but PR(0.05\\u21920.01) = 5.10 [1.0, 10.3] is not. The additive co-primary is what prevents the primary claim from becoming unidentified in strong-defense cells.\\n\\n**7.4 Stratification.** Topic-nested-within-dataset fits; per-dataset re-fit with heterogeneity statistics; dataset\\u00d7style interpreted *only* through the topic covariate (F7).\\n\\n**7.5 Utility-matched comparison.** Defense types compared at matched benign over-refusal (interpolated on the dose axis), so a defense cannot win by refusing everything.\\n\\n**7.6 Derived \\\"defense strength\\\" summary (D2).** Per type: `S = 1 \\u2212 ASR_type/ASR_none`, per style, with CIs; scalar index = mean over styles, **explicitly labeled derived and acknowledged as non-orthogonal to style** (a scalar hides the filter's style-selectivity \\u2014 the effect we care about). Published for comparability with prior work only.\\n\\n**7.7 Multiplicity.** Pre-registered confirmatory family: H1 = style \\u00d7 inference_defense; H2 = style \\u00d7 inference_defense \\u00d7 budget (**primary**); H3 = exposure novel-vs-previously-tested (binary, per D7). Everything 4-way and up \\u2014 including exposure \\u00d7 defense \\u00d7 budget \\u2014 is exploratory with FDR. Power arithmetic (\\u00a78) shows the 4-ways cannot be confirmed at feasible n, so declaring them exploratory is a correctness requirement, not a hedge.\\n\\n**7.8 Uncertainty.** Cluster bootstrap by behavior and seed; ICC/design-effect reported; per-cell n and effective sample size in every table; seed-variance separated from behavior-variance.\\n\\n**7.9 First-class gap result (D9).** `\\u0394_adapt = ASR_TierB \\u2212 ASR_TierA` per (style \\u00d7 defense \\u00d7 budget), with CI. Expected shape if adaptivity matters: \\u0394 grows with defense strength (frozen artifacts fail for reasons the attacker could have worked around) and is larger for PAIR than AutoDAN (semantic space adapts; a fixed affix cannot). Reported as a headline figure.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a78 Power (planning arithmetic, executed)\\n\\nAdditive-scale 2\\u00d72 interaction MDE = z\\u00b7\\u221a(\\u03a3 p(1\\u2212p)/n), z=2.802 (80% power, \\u03b1=.05), p\\u22480.20:\\n\\n| n/cell | 60 | 120 | 240 | 450 | 900 |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| MDE | 28.9 pp | 20.5 pp | 14.5 pp | **10.6 pp** | 7.5 pp |\\n\\nAt the standard regime (~120 behaviors \\u00d7 3 seeds per cell \\u21d2 n\\u2248360, and paired/within-behavior structure helps), detectable additive interactions are ~11\\u201313 pp. That is the honest ceiling: **medium and large interactions are detectable, 5\\u20138 pp ones are not**, which is why the design leans on the paired within-behavior structure and on the Q50/PR estimand (which pools information across the whole budget curve rather than one point) rather than pretending the 4-way is confirmable. A pre-registered simulation using Phase-0-fitted ICCs finalizes N before any confirmatory run.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a79 Cost model, regimes, decision rule (D5)\\n\\n**Primitives.** 1\\u00d7 target queries/behavior: AutoDAN canonical worst case **4800** (120\\u00d740), PAIR **400** (20\\u00d720) \\u2192 **12:1**. Realized under early stop, planning assumption ~500 vs ~400 \\u2192 **1.25:1**. Phase 0 measures which is true.\\n\\n**Structural finding that drives the whole budget (executed arithmetic).** Tier A's *replay* cost \\u2014 the entire style \\u00d7 defense \\u00d7 exposure \\u00d7 dataset contrast \\u2014 is **\\u2264 0.05M queries, under 0.2% of total**. Defense cells are essentially free once an artifact exists; **optimization is the entire bill.** Consequences: (a) the defense factor stays fully crossed and never gets fractionated; (b) Tier B, which requires re-optimizing per defense cell, is the only factor that must be rationed; (c) the budget ladder is computed by **checkpointing one 4\\u00d7 run** to read off 0.25\\u00d7 and 1\\u00d7 (planning: 19,200 vs 25,200 queries per behavior \\u2014 a 1.31\\u00d7 saving), with a small independent low-budget replicate to validate that checkpoints equal genuine independent low-budget runs (they may not, because early stopping changes the search).\\n\\n**Regimes** (per target-model \\u00d7 alignment-stage cell; planning arithmetic at realized 1\\u00d7, early stop):\\n\\n| regime | behaviors | ladder subset | seeds | Tier B (cells, behaviors) | Tier A gen | Tier A replay | Tier B | **total queries** | scored attempts |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **full** | 200 | 60 | 3 | (4, 60) @1\\u00d7+4\\u00d7 | 2.38M | 43k | 6.48M | **\\u22488.9M** | 43,200 |\\n| **standard** | 120 | 40 | 3 | (2, 40) @1\\u00d7 | 1.51M | 17k | 0.43M | **\\u22482.0M** | 17,280 |\\n| **stripped fallback** | 60 | 20 | 2 | none | 0.50M | 3k | 0 | **\\u22480.5M** | 2,880 |\\n\\nModel grid multiplies linearly: standard \\u00d78 configs \\u2248 15.7M. Judge calls = 2 \\u00d7 scored attempts (ensemble), plus human gold ~400.\\n\\n**Decision rule.** Let C = available target-query ceiling.\\n1. Always fund **stripped** first: 2 styles \\u00d7 8 defense cells \\u00d7 3 budgets \\u00d7 60 behaviors identifies **style \\u00d7 defense \\u00d7 budget** (the primary) from Tier A alone, because defense is within-behavior and replay is ~free. This is the property that makes the fallback defensible rather than crippled.\\n2. Buy, in order: seeds 2\\u21923 (behavior-level variance, cheap: replay only) \\u2192 behaviors 60\\u2192120 \\u2192 model grid 1\\u21924\\u21928 \\u2192 exposure 2\\u21923 levels \\u2192 ladder subset \\u2192 Tier B last.\\n3. **Tier B is sized by formula, not choice:** for `n_exp` optimized exposures, `S` seeds, `n_cells` adaptive defense cells and budget set B,\\n `N_B = C_remaining / [ (Q_A1 + Q_P1) \\u00b7 \\u03a3_{b\\u2208B} b \\u00b7 S \\u00b7 n_exp \\u00b7 n_cells ]`\\n (planning: at realized 1\\u00d7, C=1M, 2 cells, 1\\u00d7 only \\u21d2 N_B\\u224860; at 4 cells with 1\\u00d7+4\\u00d7 \\u21d2 N_B\\u22486.) If N_B < ~15 behaviors, Tier B is deferred entirely and the adaptivity gap (D9) is reported as **unmeasured** \\u2014 an explicit, pre-declared failure mode rather than a silently underpowered number.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a710 Controls and falsification checks\\n\\n(a) **Attack-free direct-query baseline** per defense cell \\u2192 intrinsic refusal anchor; every ASR is read relative to it. (b) **Benign paired set** \\u2192 over-refusal cost, used for \\u00a77.5 matching. (c) **Surface-form controls**: shuffled AutoDAN affix; one-shot PAIR template with the optimization loop disabled \\u2014 separates *optimization* from *surface form*; without these, \\\"attacker strength\\\" and \\\"attack style\\\" cannot be told apart. (d) **Gibberish/truncation controls** \\u2192 judge false-positive rate. (e) **Held-out attack seeds** \\u2192 artifact out-of-sample generalization. (f) **Judge-judge agreement by style** \\u2192 if style\\u00d7defense interactions appear with judge J1 and vanish with J2, they are scoring artifacts. (g) **Checkpoint-vs-independent-budget replicate** \\u2192 validates the 1.31\\u00d7 ladder saving.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a711 Feasibility\\n\\n**Nothing is provisioned.** Verified: `/workspace` holds one file; no code, no weights, no data, no judge, no GPU, no network, no `torch`/`numpy`/`statsmodels`. The design must be executed elsewhere.\\n\\n**Must be built:** (1) harm-benchmark acquisition + license/usage-policy review; (2) benign paired set; (3) local serving for the model grid; (4) **AutoDAN reimplementation** (official code unavailable offline \\u2014 highest fidelity risk; a weak reimplementation understates token-level ASR and would *manufacture* a style \\u00d7 filter interaction); (5) PAIR harness + attacker-LLM serving; (6) input filter (perplexity + obfuscation classifier \\u2014 needs training data); (7) moderation classifier; (8) strengthened-alignment checkpoint; (9) judge ensemble + stripping pipeline + gold-set annotation tooling; (10) provenance ledger; (11) artifact storage under a red-team access policy.\\n\\n**Riskiest dependency: the strengthened-alignment checkpoint (A5).** Without it `alignment_stage` collapses and roughly half the question (\\\"RLHF-baseline vs strengthened alignment\\\") is unanswerable. Degradation ladder, in order:\\n1. **Official hardened successor** of the same model (cheapest; confounded with version/training-vintage).\\n2. **In-house safety fine-tune (SFT/DPO) of an open base** \\u2014 the only option supporting the *exposure\\u00d7defense* manipulation (the defense can be genuinely fitted on the previously-tested library). Costs a training run; confounded with the fine-tuning recipe.\\n3. **Alignment as measured covariate, not manipulated factor** (e.g. attack-free refusal rate) \\u2014 cheap, but post-hoc, and must be labeled *derived/associational*; the causal claim dies.\\n4. **Drop the axis.** Design becomes inference-defense-only: style \\u00d7 inference_defense \\u00d7 dose \\u00d7 budget \\u00d7 exposure survives intact and H1/H2/H3 stand; the deliverable states that the alignment half is unaddressed.\\nNote that only option 2 licenses the clean exposure\\u00d7defense-exposure design; under 1/3/4 the novelty effect stays confounded with the defender's unknown training-data exposure (residual of F5).\\n\\n**Other risks.** Benchmark contamination (uncontrollable; drives the `publicized`-level caveat). AutoDAN fidelity gap (mitigated by reproducing the published ASR on the paper's own setting before any cell is trusted \\u2014 a required gate). Harmful-content policy and disclosure obligations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a712 Optional identification probe (beyond fixed requirements \\u2014 D3/D4; excluded from the primary model)\\n\\nAccess is confounded with style by construction. One labelled sensitivity arm breaks the confound using a 2\\u00d72 completion: **white-box token-level comparator** (gradient-based affix search on the same affix-length/tokenization constraints as AutoDAN) and **black-box prompt-level comparator** (iterative semantic attacker, PAIR-matched budget), run on a small behavior subset (\\u226430 behaviors, 1\\u00d7 budget, 3 defense cells) with **no AutoDAN/PAIR modification**, reported separately as \\\"style vs access decomposition,\\\" never pooled into H1\\u2013H3. Expected diagnostic value: if the white-box token-level arm reproduces AutoDAN's filter vulnerability, the style effect is really an access/surface effect; if not, token-level natural-language morphology is doing independent work. Flagged as a cost add-on of the same order as Tier B.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a713 Limitations / non-identifiability register\\n\\nAccess \\u2261 style (declared, D3). Defense robustness \\u2261 non-adaptivity within Tier A alone (resolved only by Tier B, which may be deferred \\u2192 gap reported unmeasured). Publicized-level exposure \\u2261 defender pretraining contamination (hence D7's binary primary). Attacker strength beyond realized query count (attacker-side FLOPs) is reported, not modeled. Dataset \\u2261 topic-mix bundle (topic covariate only partially separates). Interaction direction is scale-dependent by construction (\\u00a77.3). Model-grid n of 2 families \\u00d7 2 scales supports *description* of model heterogeneity, not inference over the model population. Human gold-set size bounds the judge-correction precision.\\n\\n## \\u00a714 Ethics and handling\\nRed-team context, restricted artifact storage, no release of working artifacts, benchmark usage-policy compliance, pre-publication provider disclosure review, and human annotation of harmful content done with appropriate reviewer support.\\n\\n## \\u00a715 Reporting checklist (each item is a deliverable)\\n4-class outcome table per cell \\u00b7 ASR with all-attempts denominator **and** the blocked/refusal decomposition \\u00b7 ASR@k curves + Q50/PR/erosion slopes with cluster-bootstrap CIs \\u00b7 additive **and** multiplicative interaction estimates \\u00b7 Tier A \\u2212 Tier B gap \\u00b7 derived defense-strength summary labeled derived \\u00b7 benign over-refusal alongside every ASR \\u00b7 judge disagreement + gold-set error rates + corrected-ASR refit \\u00b7 degraded-single-judge comparison \\u00b7 per-cell n, ICC, MDE \\u00b7 provenance ledger \\u00b7 regime actually run and why.\\n\", \"evidence\": \"**Environment verification (all executed):**\\n1. `ls -la /workspace` + `find /workspace -maxdepth 3` \\u2192 only `task.json` (637 B). No repo.\\n2. `cat /workspace/task.json` \\u2192 question + `\\\"track.md\\\": \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"` No setup docs.\\n3. `python3 -c \\\"import torch,transformers\\\"` \\u2192 ModuleNotFoundError; `pip list` \\u2192 system packages only.\\n4. Explicit import probe \\u2192 numpy, scipy, statsmodels, pandas, openai, anthropic all MISSING; Python 3.14.4.\\n5. `nvidia-smi` \\u2192 fails, no driver (no GPU). `nproc`=224, RAM ~2 TB.\\n6. `ls /data /models /opt`, `ls ~`, `~/.cache/huggingface` \\u2192 nothing (no weights/data/cache).\\n7. `find / -xdev` for track.md / setup_1* / *neurips* \\u2192 empty (setup_17/18 unreadable, as researcher confirms); `.git` \\u2192 none; *autodan*/*pair*/*jailbreak* \\u2192 none (no harnesses).\\n8. urllib probe to huggingface.co \\u2192 URLError name resolution (confirms network disabled).\\n\\n**Planning arithmetic executed (these are design computations, not experimental results):**\\n9. `/tmp/mech.py` \\u2014 denominator reversal: none 100 attempts/90 delivered/30 harmful \\u2192 ASR_all 0.300, ASR_delivered 0.333; filter 100/40/15 \\u2192 ASR_all 0.150 (defense halves ASR) but ASR_delivered **0.375** (defense appears harmful). Confirms the mechanical reversal claim in \\u00a74.\\n10. `/tmp/cost.py` \\u2014 query primitives: AutoDAN 1\\u00d7=4800, PAIR 1\\u00d7=400 (ratio 12\\u00d7); Q50=ln0.5/ln(1\\u2212p) table (p=0.01\\u219269, 0.02\\u219234.3, 0.05\\u219213.5, 0.10\\u21926.58, 0.30\\u21921.94); protection ratios (0.30\\u21920.10 = 3.39\\u00d7, 0.30\\u21920.05 = 6.95\\u00d7, 0.30\\u21920.01 = 35.5\\u00d7).\\n11. `/tmp/model.py` \\u2014 **AutoDAN:PAIR canonical ratio 12\\u00d7**; checkpointed budget ladder costs 19,200 vs 25,200 queries/behavior = 1.31\\u00d7 saving; Tier B feasible behaviors N_B vs ceiling C (C=1M, 2 cells, 1\\u00d7 \\u2192 N_B\\u224824; 4 cells with 1\\u00d7+4\\u00d7 \\u2192 N_B\\u22482.4; C=5M \\u2192 120 / 12; C=20M \\u2192 481 / 48).\\n12. `/tmp/model2.py` \\u2014 realized-vs-canonical ratio (500 vs 400 = 1.25\\u00d7); regime table at realized 1\\u00d7: full \\u22488.9M queries (43,200 scored attempts), standard \\u22482.0M (17,280), stripped \\u22480.5M (2,880); **replay cost \\u226443k = <0.2% of total** \\u2192 defense factor stays fully crossed, optimization is the whole bill, Tier B is the only rationed factor; model-grid multiplier \\u00d71/\\u00d74/\\u00d78 \\u2192 2.0M/7.8M/15.7M.\\n13. `/tmp/power.py` \\u2014 additive 2\\u00d72 interaction MDE at 80% power/\\u03b1=.05, p\\u22480.2: 28.9pp (n=60), 14.5pp (240), 10.6pp (450), 7.5pp (900); per-cell multinomial SE 0.052/0.040/0.028 at Nb=60/100/200; delta-method PR CIs \\u2192 PR(0.30\\u21920.05)=6.95 [3.85,10.06] usable but PR(0.05\\u21920.01)=5.10 [1.00,10.27] at n=450 and [1.00,15.11] at n=120, i.e. multiplicative scale becomes unidentified in strong-defense cells \\u2192 justifies the additive co-primary.\\n\\nNo LLM, model, dataset, or attack implementation was run; no outcomes about model behavior are claimed anywhere in the design.\", \"assumptions\": [\"Setup_17/setup_18 are unreadable to both parties, so NO model, dataset, defense, judge, or hyperparameter choice in this design is attributed to the source; all are researcher directives (D-table) or my assumptions (A-table).\", \"A1: target model families/sizes/checkpoints unspecified; design assumes >=2 open-weight families x >=2 scales locally served.\", \"A2: harm benchmarks and the benign paired set unspecified; named as slots, not choices.\", \"A3: judge families and versions unspecified.\", \"A4: canonical 1x budgets assumed AutoDAN 120 gen x 40 pop (4800 queries) and PAIR N=20 x M=20 (400 queries), with realized/early-stopped cost assumed much closer to parity (~500 vs ~400); Phase 0 measures which holds.\", \"A5: a strengthened-alignment checkpoint exists (or can be produced) for at least one family - flagged as the riskiest dependency with a four-step degradation ladder.\", \"A6: i.i.d. attempts within a campaign is used ONLY as an interpretive anchor for Q50; Q50 itself is estimated empirically.\", \"A7: benchmark licensing and permission to store/evaluate jailbreak artifacts in a red-team setting are assumed.\", \"Cost-model figures are parametric planning arithmetic at a stated realized-1x basis; they scale linearly with the model grid and must be recomputed once a compute ceiling C is known.\", \"Tier B (adaptive attack) may be deferred entirely if C is too small; the adaptivity gap is then reported as unmeasured rather than estimated underpowered.\", \"AutoDAN must be reimplemented offline, so its fidelity to the published method is an assumption gated by a reproduction check before any cell is trusted.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Access (white-box vs black-box) remains perfectly confounded with attack style under the fixed AutoDAN/PAIR requirement; declared non-identifiable, with only the optional section-12 probe able to separate them.\", \"Tier A alone confounds defense robustness with attacker non-adaptivity; only Tier B resolves it and Tier B may be unaffordable, in which case the D9 gap is reported unmeasured.\", \"Publicized exposure level remains confounded with defender pretraining contamination; this is why the primary contrast is pre-registered binary (novel vs previously-tested).\", \"Judge style-bias is the dominant validity threat: a single judge mis-scores disfluent AutoDAN and fluent hedged PAIR outputs in opposite directions, which can manufacture the headline style x filter interaction. Mitigated by two-family ensemble, pre-judging stripping, stratified gold set, corrected-ASR refit, judge-overfitting audit, and the explicit degraded single-judge sensitivity condition - not eliminated.\", \"Whether AutoDAN and PAIR really differ 12x or ~1.25x in realized query cost is unknown; the design's cost model changes materially depending on Phase-0 measurement.\", \"Interaction sign/scale dependence is structural: near 0/1 ASR the multiplicative protection ratio becomes unidentified (planning CIs show this), so additive and multiplicative scales must both be reported and divergence treated as a finding.\", \"With 2 families x 2 scales, model heterogeneity is descriptive only; model x defense interactions cannot support population inference over models.\", \"Topic-nested-within-dataset covariate only partially separates dataset effects from topic-mix effects (F7 residual).\", \"Detectable additive interactions are ~11-13 pp at the standard regime; true interactions of 5-8 pp will not be resolved, which is why 4-way interactions are declared exploratory.\", \"The 1.31x checkpointed-ladder saving assumes low-budget checkpoints equal independent low-budget runs; early stopping may break this, so a validation replicate is built into the design.\"], \"stage\": \"result\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-b31fab96-1c54-4fcc-bec9-fde1b3f3aa98", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "end_researcher_turn: {\"answer\": \"# Combined Jailbreak Techniques \\u00d7 ASR: Experiment Design (design-only)\\n\\n**Status.** No experiment run, none possible here (no network, no GPU, no ML stack, no code, no data, no weights \\u2014 verified by inspection). Everything below is a specification. Every number labeled *planning* is arithmetic I actually executed; every number about LLM behavior is an assumption or an illustrative placeholder, never a result.\\n\\n**Corrections to my earlier outline, stated explicitly:** (a) I wrote \\\"PAIR 20 iters \\u00d7 3 streams \\u2248 60 queries\\\"; canonical PAIR is N=20 attacker streams \\u00d7 M=20 iterations \\u21d2 \\u2264400 target queries with early stop. (b) The premise that AutoDAN and PAIR have \\\"very different compute profiles\\\" is **only true at canonical worst case (4800 vs 400 = 12\\u00d7)** and largely **evaporates under early stopping (planning: 500 vs 400 \\u2248 1.25\\u00d7)**. So the compute asymmetry is a quantity to be *measured in Phase 0*, not assumed. Phase 0 exists for this reason.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a71 Fixed requirements vs. directives vs. assumptions\\n\\n| # | Item | Status |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| R1 | Token-level attack = **AutoDAN** | **Fixed (brief/researcher)** |\\n| R2 | Prompt-level attack = **PAIR** | **Fixed (brief/researcher)** |\\n| R3 | Design-only; do not run; do not claim results | **Fixed** |\\n| R4 | Outcome measured as ASR | **Fixed (brief's question)** |\\n| D1 | Ordinal defense ladder replaced by `alignment_stage \\u00d7 inference_defense(type\\u00d7dose)` | Researcher directive |\\n| D2 | Publish a *derived*, clearly-labeled post-hoc \\\"defense strength\\\" summary (within-type ASR suppression) | Researcher directive |\\n| D3 | Core design not expanded; **access declared non-identifiable** in primary analysis | Researcher directive |\\n| D4 | Optional identification probe allowed, labelled, outside primary model | Researcher directive |\\n| D5 | Parametric cost model + 2\\u20133 named regimes + decision rule; Tier B sized as function of ceiling | Researcher directive |\\n| D6 | Harm benchmarks + topic-nested stratification + benign paired over-refusal set | Researcher directive |\\n| D7 | Exposure: 3 levels reported, **primary contrast pre-registered binary (novel vs previously-tested)** | Researcher directive |\\n| D8 | \\u22652 open-weight families \\u00d7 \\u22652 scales; two-family judge ensemble; blinding by artifact stripping; stratified human gold set; error-rate sensitivity refit; explicit degraded single-judge variant | Researcher directive |\\n| D9 | Tier A \\u2212 Tier B gap reported as first-class result | Researcher directive |\\n| **A1** | **Which** models (families/sizes/checkpoints) | **Assumption \\u2014 unspecified, not source-attributed** |\\n| **A2** | Which harm benchmarks, which benign set | **Assumption** |\\n| **A3** | Judge model families; judge versions | **Assumption** |\\n| **A4** | Canonical 1\\u00d7 hyperparameters (AutoDAN 120 gen \\u00d7 40 pop; PAIR N=20, M=20) | **Assumption** |\\n| **A5** | A strengthened-alignment checkpoint exists for \\u22651 family | **Assumption \\u2014 highest-risk (see \\u00a711)** |\\n| **A6** | Per-attempt independence within an attack campaign (used only as an interpretive anchor) | **Assumption** |\\n| **A7** | Harm-benchmark licensing + jailbreak-artifact handling permission | **Assumption** |\\n| **A8** | setup_17/setup_18 exist but are unreadable to both parties; **no setup detail below is attributed to them** | Verified constraint |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a72 Factors, finalized\\n\\n**Attack style** (2, fixed by R1/R2): AutoDAN (token/GA-level, fluency- and perplexity-constrained natural-language affix) vs PAIR (attacker-LLM iterative semantic prompt refinement). Whole-plot factor; sets per-run compute profile and output morphology.\\n\\n**Attacker strength** (3 levels: 0.25\\u00d7 / 1\\u00d7 / 4\\u00d7), **measured in one common currency: target-model queries per behavior**, with attacker-side FLOPs reported as a *separate* cost axis (PAIR pays attacker-LLM queries \\u2248 target queries; AutoDAN pays a local scorer). Two ladders, never conflated:\\n- **Canonical ladder** (worst-case search space: generations\\u00d7population vs iterations\\u00d7streams)\\n- **Realized ladder** (queries actually consumed under early stop)\\nPhase 0 measures the realized distribution; the budget-curve estimand (\\u00a75) is reported against realized queries, which is what makes cross-style \\\"attacker strength\\\" comparable (resolves my earlier F6).\\n\\n**Defense** (8 primary cells) = `alignment_stage`(2: shipped RLHF baseline, strengthened) \\u00d7 `inference_defense`(4 types: none / static system-prompt hardening / input-side filter / output-side moderation). Plus **within-type dose**: 2\\u20133 doses per active type (e.g. filter at 3 perplexity/flag-rate percentiles; moderation at 2 decision thresholds; 2 system-prompt variants). Doses are **calibrated to place each defense type on a common over-refusal axis**, so the headline defense comparison can be read at matched benign-utility cost (\\u00a77.5). \\\"Defense strength\\\" as a scalar is *not* a design primitive; it is published only as the derived summary in \\u00a77.6.\\n\\n**Exposure / previously-tested tricks** (3 levels; primary contrast binary):\\n- `novel` \\u2014 artifacts optimized in-study, absent from any public library and from the defense-fitting data (ledger-verified, canary-tagged)\\n- `previously-tested` \\u2014 artifacts harvested from an earlier phase of *this* study against this target, then replayed (defender has demonstrably seen them)\\n- `publicized` \\u2014 frozen snapshot of a public library with documented dates; **reported, excluded from the primary contrast** (contamination caveat: pretrained defenders may already have seen it)\\nPipeline and query budget are held fixed across levels; only provenance varies. Confound control: artifacts are **matched on optimizer fitness** (so novelty is not a proxy for attack quality) and a **provenance ledger** records, per artifact, its similarity to anything in the defense-fitting data \\u2014 used as a measured covariate.\\n\\n**Datasets** (blocking): harm-benchmark query sets, **topic nested within dataset** as stratifying covariate; plus a **benign paired utility set** scored on the same items.\\n\\n**Declared non-identifiable and not estimated in the primary model (D3):** white-box vs black-box *access* \\u2014 perfectly confounded with style given R1/R2. Reported as a limitation; the \\u00a712 probe is the only attempt at separation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a73 Design structure\\n\\n**Phase 0 \\u2014 calibration (small, no hypotheses).** Each style \\u00d7 each benchmark, ~25 behaviors, canonical settings run to convergence. Products: realized-queries-to-success distribution (sets realized 1\\u00d7), the measured AutoDAN:PAIR compute ratio (tests the 12\\u00d7 vs 1.25\\u00d7 question), attack-fitness distribution for exposure matching, and initial judge\\u2013human disagreement rates by style.\\n\\n**Tier A \\u2014 frozen-artifact transfer matrix (the primary factorial, cheap).** Optimize each artifact once against a *fixed reference configuration*, then replay the frozen artifact across all 8 defense cells \\u00d7 doses. Fully crossed at the artifact level: 2 style \\u00d7 3 exposure \\u00d7 8 defense \\u00d7 dose \\u00d7 3 datasets \\u00d7 behaviors \\u00d7 seeds.\\n**Tier B \\u2014 adaptive attack (the honest estimator, expensive).** Attacker optimizes *against the actual deployed defense*, re-run per defense cell. Deliberately fractional; sizing is a function of the compute ceiling (\\u00a79), never an arbitrary constant.\\n\\n**Nested vs crossed (explicit).** Within-style attacker knobs (GA population; PAIR stream count and attacker-LLM capability) are **nested in style** and never entered as crossed factors \\u2014 they are undefined or incommensurable across styles. Everything else is crossed.\\n\\n**Unit of analysis.** The *attack attempt*: (behavior \\u00d7 style \\u00d7 exposure \\u00d7 defense-cell \\u00d7 dose \\u00d7 seed). Behavior is the clustering/generalization unit; **defense and exposure are within-behavior** (paired), which is where most of the design's efficiency comes from. Random effects: behavior, behavior\\u00d7defense, model, seed.\\n\\n**What Tier A alone can and cannot say.** Tier A answers \\\"does a fixed artifact transfer across defenses?\\\" It cannot answer \\\"does a stronger attacker defeat a stronger defense when the attacker adapts?\\\" \\u2014 that is exactly why the **Tier A \\u2212 Tier B gap is a first-class reported estimand** (D9), not a footnote: it quantifies adaptivity bias in the frozen-transfer literature that Tier A-style protocols represent.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a74 THE LOAD-BEARING SCORING DECISION: 4-class outcome + all-attempts-initiated denominator\\n\\n**Outcome is multinomial per attempt, with a mandatory logged class:**\\n1. `blocked` \\u2014 stopped by input-side filter before reaching the model\\n2. `refused` \\u2014 reached the model, model declined\\n3. `off-target` \\u2014 answered, but not with the harmful content (includes incoherent/degraded output)\\n4. `harmful` \\u2014 harmful completion (judge-confirmed)\\n\\n**Denominator: every attempt initiated. Filter-blocked attempts stay in the denominator.**\\n\\n**Why the alternative mechanically reverses the effect under test.** If blocked attempts are excluded, the denominator silently conditions on surviving the filter. Filters block *disproportionately the weakest* attempts, so delivered-only ASR is a post-treatment selected quantity. Executed arithmetic (planning illustration, not data):\\n\\n| condition | attempts | delivered | blocked | harmful | **ASR_all** | ASR_delivered |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| none | 100 | 90 | 10 | 30 | **0.300** | 0.333 |\\n| input filter | 100 | 40 | 60 | 15 | **0.150** | **0.375** |\\n\\nWith all-attempts denominators the filter halves ASR (0.300\\u21920.150). With delivered-only denominators the same filter *raises* ASR (0.333\\u21920.375) and the defense appears to have made the model **less** safe. The reversal is not noise; it is selection created by the scoring rule, and it points precisely at the style\\u00d7filter interaction the question asks about \\u2014 the cell where AutoDAN affixes are blocked and fluent PAIR prompts are not. Any delivered-only analysis of this design is invalid, full stop.\\n\\nThe 4-class structure also makes ASR **decomposable**: `ASR = P(delivered) \\u00d7 P(harmful | delivered)`. The log-additive form attributes a defense's suppression to the *blocking leg* vs the *refusal leg* \\u2014 the difference between \\\"the wall caught it\\\" and \\\"the model refused.\\\"\\n\\n**Reported ASR variants.** (i) per-attempt ASR (all-attempts denominator); (ii) **ASR@k** per behavior = P(\\u22651 success in k attempts), measured empirically, the attacker's realistic objective; (iii) ASR-vs-realized-query curve; (iv) paired benign over-refusal rate.\\n\\n**Eligibility screen.** Behaviors the model already complies with attack-free are flagged, not deleted from some cells: the screen is computed **once per (model \\u00d7 dataset), defense-free**, and applied identically everywhere; screen-out rates are reported per dataset/topic, and both screened and unscreened primary results are given.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a75 Primary estimand: budget-curve reframing (the primary statement of interaction dynamics)\\n\\nASR at a single budget is not comparable across styles because ASR is monotone in queries. So the headline quantities are **curve quantities**:\\n\\n- **ASR@k curve** per (style \\u00d7 defense-cell \\u00d7 dose \\u00d7 dataset), measured empirically.\\n- **Q50 = the query budget at which ASR@k first reaches 0.50** (interpolated; CI by cluster bootstrap). Reported per cell.\\n- **Protection ratio PR = Q50(defense) / Q50(none)** \\u2014 *\\\"how many queries does this defense buy.\\\"*\\n- **PR erosion slope: d PR / d log(budget)** \\u2014 *\\\"does the protection survive a stronger attacker?\\\"*\\n\\n**Primary interaction statement (H2): \\u0394 log PR between styles, and its slope over log-budget.** I.e., does a given defense buy AutoDAN 3\\u00d7 more queries than it buys PAIR, and does that differential survive a 4\\u00d7 attacker? This is scale-meaningful, survives ceiling/floor problems far better than a raw ASR\\u00d7ASR interaction, and is what \\\"attacker power \\u00d7 defense robustness dynamics\\\" actually means operationally.\\n\\nReference anchor only (assumption A6): under i.i.d. attempts, Q50 = ln0.5/ln(1\\u2212p). Planning values: p=0.01\\u219269, 0.02\\u219234.3, 0.05\\u219213.5, 0.10\\u21926.6, 0.30\\u21921.9. Q50 is estimated **empirically** because GA populations and PAIR streams are positively dependent; the systematic gap between empirical and i.i.d. Q50 is itself reported as a within-campaign dependence diagnostic.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a76 Scoring and judging\\n\\n**Pipeline.** (1) Cheap deterministic pass: refusal-pattern + harmful-content keyword rules \\u2192 `refused` vs candidate. (2) LLM judge on a HarmBench-style semantic rubric \\u2192 4-class label. (3) Human gold set.\\n\\n**Style-bias problem, stated plainly.** AutoDAN output tends to be disfluent or partially-compliant; PAIR output tends to be fluent and hedged. A single judge mis-scores these in *opposite directions*, which fabricates a style \\u00d7 defense interaction out of nothing. This is the largest single threat to validity.\\n\\n**Controls.**\\n- **Two-family judge ensemble**, majority-of-3 with the rule pass as arbiter; disagreement logged as a measured quantity.\\n- **Blinding:** the adversarial affix/preamble and any condition-revealing formatting (length, scaffolding, attack markers) are **stripped before judging**. The judge sees only (original harmful intent, model response). It never sees which cell generated the response.\\n- **Human gold set**, ~400 items **stratified over style \\u00d7 defense \\u00d7 response-fluency decile**, deliberately over-sampling AutoDAN disfluent outputs. Yields per-condition sensitivity/specificity.\\n- **Sensitivity refit:** observed ASR corrected per condition by measured judge error, ASR_corrected = (ASR_obs + Spec \\u2212 1)/(Sens + Spec \\u2212 1), reported alongside raw ASR for every headline contrast. A conclusion that survives raw but not corrected scoring is reported as judge-dependent.\\n- **AutoDAN judge-overfitting audit** (mandatory): AutoDAN's optimizer can overfit to the scoring function. Two checks \\u2014 (a) re-score artifacts optimized against judge J1 using judge J2 and the gold set (transfer degradation = overfit magnitude); (b) \\\"gibberish controls\\\" (random affix, truncated outputs) run through the judge to measure false-positive rate directly. In-loop fitness scoring and final scoring use **different judge instances/versions**.\\n- **Degraded single-judge variant (explicit, D8):** one judge family, no gold set, rule pass only. Reported as a *named sensitivity condition*, not as the primary. Predicted and tested consequence: with a single judge the style\\u00d7filter interaction is biased toward zero on the AutoDAN arm because blocked/incoherent outputs get mislabeled; the degraded variant's divergence from ensemble scoring is quantified so the reader can calibrate prior single-judge ASR literature.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a77 Analysis plan\\n\\n**7.1 Primary (multinomial).** Mixed-effects multinomial logistic on attempt-level outcomes, reference class `harmful`:\\n`outcome ~ style * inference_defense * dose * budget * exposure * dataset + topic(style:dataset) + alignment_stage + (1+inference_defense|behavior) + (1|model) + (1|seed)`.\\nReports predicted marginal means + 95% CIs per cell (not p-value triage), and the blocking/refusal decomposition of \\u00a74.\\n\\n**7.2 Curve estimands.** Per-cell ASR@k curves and Q50/PR/erosion-slope (\\u00a75) with cluster-bootstrap CIs over behaviors and seeds. **This is the primary inferential surface.**\\n\\n**7.3 Both scales, pre-registered (F8).** Because ASR\\u21921 under defense-none and ASR\\u21920 under moderation, multiplicative interaction is interpretable only alongside additive:\\n- **Multiplicative:** ratios of ORs, and PR ratios on the log scale (primary, per \\u00a75).\\n- **Additive:** marginal risk-difference contrasts and RERI on the ASR scale.\\nDivergence between the two is reported as a finding, not reconciled silently. Planning arithmetic showing why both are needed: PR CIs blow up at low p \\u2014 at n=450/cell, PR(0.30\\u21920.05) = 6.95 [3.9, 10.1] is usable, but PR(0.05\\u21920.01) = 5.10 [1.0, 10.3] is not. The additive co-primary is what prevents the primary claim from becoming unidentified in strong-defense cells.\\n\\n**7.4 Stratification.** Topic-nested-within-dataset fits; per-dataset re-fit with heterogeneity statistics; dataset\\u00d7style interpreted *only* through the topic covariate (F7).\\n\\n**7.5 Utility-matched comparison.** Defense types compared at matched benign over-refusal (interpolated on the dose axis), so a defense cannot win by refusing everything.\\n\\n**7.6 Derived \\\"defense strength\\\" summary (D2).** Per type: `S = 1 \\u2212 ASR_type/ASR_none`, per style, with CIs; scalar index = mean over styles, **explicitly labeled derived and acknowledged as non-orthogonal to style** (a scalar hides the filter's style-selectivity \\u2014 the effect we care about). Published for comparability with prior work only.\\n\\n**7.7 Multiplicity.** Pre-registered confirmatory family: H1 = style \\u00d7 inference_defense; H2 = style \\u00d7 inference_defense \\u00d7 budget (**primary**); H3 = exposure novel-vs-previously-tested (binary, per D7). Everything 4-way and up \\u2014 including exposure \\u00d7 defense \\u00d7 budget \\u2014 is exploratory with FDR. Power arithmetic (\\u00a78) shows the 4-ways cannot be confirmed at feasible n, so declaring them exploratory is a correctness requirement, not a hedge.\\n\\n**7.8 Uncertainty.** Cluster bootstrap by behavior and seed; ICC/design-effect reported; per-cell n and effective sample size in every table; seed-variance separated from behavior-variance.\\n\\n**7.9 First-class gap result (D9).** `\\u0394_adapt = ASR_TierB \\u2212 ASR_TierA` per (style \\u00d7 defense \\u00d7 budget), with CI. Expected shape if adaptivity matters: \\u0394 grows with defense strength (frozen artifacts fail for reasons the attacker could have worked around) and is larger for PAIR than AutoDAN (semantic space adapts; a fixed affix cannot). Reported as a headline figure.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a78 Power (planning arithmetic, executed)\\n\\nAdditive-scale 2\\u00d72 interaction MDE = z\\u00b7\\u221a(\\u03a3 p(1\\u2212p)/n), z=2.802 (80% power, \\u03b1=.05), p\\u22480.20:\\n\\n| n/cell | 60 | 120 | 240 | 450 | 900 |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| MDE | 28.9 pp | 20.5 pp | 14.5 pp | **10.6 pp** | 7.5 pp |\\n\\nAt the standard regime (~120 behaviors \\u00d7 3 seeds per cell \\u21d2 n\\u2248360, and paired/within-behavior structure helps), detectable additive interactions are ~11\\u201313 pp. That is the honest ceiling: **medium and large interactions are detectable, 5\\u20138 pp ones are not**, which is why the design leans on the paired within-behavior structure and on the Q50/PR estimand (which pools information across the whole budget curve rather than one point) rather than pretending the 4-way is confirmable. A pre-registered simulation using Phase-0-fitted ICCs finalizes N before any confirmatory run.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a79 Cost model, regimes, decision rule (D5)\\n\\n**Primitives.** 1\\u00d7 target queries/behavior: AutoDAN canonical worst case **4800** (120\\u00d740), PAIR **400** (20\\u00d720) \\u2192 **12:1**. Realized under early stop, planning assumption ~500 vs ~400 \\u2192 **1.25:1**. Phase 0 measures which is true.\\n\\n**Structural finding that drives the whole budget (executed arithmetic).** Tier A's *replay* cost \\u2014 the entire style \\u00d7 defense \\u00d7 exposure \\u00d7 dataset contrast \\u2014 is **\\u2264 0.05M queries, under 0.2% of total**. Defense cells are essentially free once an artifact exists; **optimization is the entire bill.** Consequences: (a) the defense factor stays fully crossed and never gets fractionated; (b) Tier B, which requires re-optimizing per defense cell, is the only factor that must be rationed; (c) the budget ladder is computed by **checkpointing one 4\\u00d7 run** to read off 0.25\\u00d7 and 1\\u00d7 (planning: 19,200 vs 25,200 queries per behavior \\u2014 a 1.31\\u00d7 saving), with a small independent low-budget replicate to validate that checkpoints equal genuine independent low-budget runs (they may not, because early stopping changes the search).\\n\\n**Regimes** (per target-model \\u00d7 alignment-stage cell; planning arithmetic at realized 1\\u00d7, early stop):\\n\\n| regime | behaviors | ladder subset | seeds | Tier B (cells, behaviors) | Tier A gen | Tier A replay | Tier B | **total queries** | scored attempts |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **full** | 200 | 60 | 3 | (4, 60) @1\\u00d7+4\\u00d7 | 2.38M | 43k | 6.48M | **\\u22488.9M** | 43,200 |\\n| **standard** | 120 | 40 | 3 | (2, 40) @1\\u00d7 | 1.51M | 17k | 0.43M | **\\u22482.0M** | 17,280 |\\n| **stripped fallback** | 60 | 20 | 2 | none | 0.50M | 3k | 0 | **\\u22480.5M** | 2,880 |\\n\\nModel grid multiplies linearly: standard \\u00d78 configs \\u2248 15.7M. Judge calls = 2 \\u00d7 scored attempts (ensemble), plus human gold ~400.\\n\\n**Decision rule.** Let C = available target-query ceiling.\\n1. Always fund **stripped** first: 2 styles \\u00d7 8 defense cells \\u00d7 3 budgets \\u00d7 60 behaviors identifies **style \\u00d7 defense \\u00d7 budget** (the primary) from Tier A alone, because defense is within-behavior and replay is ~free. This is the property that makes the fallback defensible rather than crippled.\\n2. Buy, in order: seeds 2\\u21923 (behavior-level variance, cheap: replay only) \\u2192 behaviors 60\\u2192120 \\u2192 model grid 1\\u21924\\u21928 \\u2192 exposure 2\\u21923 levels \\u2192 ladder subset \\u2192 Tier B last.\\n3. **Tier B is sized by formula, not choice:** for `n_exp` optimized exposures, `S` seeds, `n_cells` adaptive defense cells and budget set B,\\n `N_B = C_remaining / [ (Q_A1 + Q_P1) \\u00b7 \\u03a3_{b\\u2208B} b \\u00b7 S \\u00b7 n_exp \\u00b7 n_cells ]`\\n (planning: at realized 1\\u00d7, C=1M, 2 cells, 1\\u00d7 only \\u21d2 N_B\\u224860; at 4 cells with 1\\u00d7+4\\u00d7 \\u21d2 N_B\\u22486.) If N_B < ~15 behaviors, Tier B is deferred entirely and the adaptivity gap (D9) is reported as **unmeasured** \\u2014 an explicit, pre-declared failure mode rather than a silently underpowered number.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a710 Controls and falsification checks\\n\\n(a) **Attack-free direct-query baseline** per defense cell \\u2192 intrinsic refusal anchor; every ASR is read relative to it. (b) **Benign paired set** \\u2192 over-refusal cost, used for \\u00a77.5 matching. (c) **Surface-form controls**: shuffled AutoDAN affix; one-shot PAIR template with the optimization loop disabled \\u2014 separates *optimization* from *surface form*; without these, \\\"attacker strength\\\" and \\\"attack style\\\" cannot be told apart. (d) **Gibberish/truncation controls** \\u2192 judge false-positive rate. (e) **Held-out attack seeds** \\u2192 artifact out-of-sample generalization. (f) **Judge-judge agreement by style** \\u2192 if style\\u00d7defense interactions appear with judge J1 and vanish with J2, they are scoring artifacts. (g) **Checkpoint-vs-independent-budget replicate** \\u2192 validates the 1.31\\u00d7 ladder saving.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a711 Feasibility\\n\\n**Nothing is provisioned.** Verified: `/workspace` holds one file; no code, no weights, no data, no judge, no GPU, no network, no `torch`/`numpy`/`statsmodels`. The design must be executed elsewhere.\\n\\n**Must be built:** (1) harm-benchmark acquisition + license/usage-policy review; (2) benign paired set; (3) local serving for the model grid; (4) **AutoDAN reimplementation** (official code unavailable offline \\u2014 highest fidelity risk; a weak reimplementation understates token-level ASR and would *manufacture* a style \\u00d7 filter interaction); (5) PAIR harness + attacker-LLM serving; (6) input filter (perplexity + obfuscation classifier \\u2014 needs training data); (7) moderation classifier; (8) strengthened-alignment checkpoint; (9) judge ensemble + stripping pipeline + gold-set annotation tooling; (10) provenance ledger; (11) artifact storage under a red-team access policy.\\n\\n**Riskiest dependency: the strengthened-alignment checkpoint (A5).** Without it `alignment_stage` collapses and roughly half the question (\\\"RLHF-baseline vs strengthened alignment\\\") is unanswerable. Degradation ladder, in order:\\n1. **Official hardened successor** of the same model (cheapest; confounded with version/training-vintage).\\n2. **In-house safety fine-tune (SFT/DPO) of an open base** \\u2014 the only option supporting the *exposure\\u00d7defense* manipulation (the defense can be genuinely fitted on the previously-tested library). Costs a training run; confounded with the fine-tuning recipe.\\n3. **Alignment as measured covariate, not manipulated factor** (e.g. attack-free refusal rate) \\u2014 cheap, but post-hoc, and must be labeled *derived/associational*; the causal claim dies.\\n4. **Drop the axis.** Design becomes inference-defense-only: style \\u00d7 inference_defense \\u00d7 dose \\u00d7 budget \\u00d7 exposure survives intact and H1/H2/H3 stand; the deliverable states that the alignment half is unaddressed.\\nNote that only option 2 licenses the clean exposure\\u00d7defense-exposure design; under 1/3/4 the novelty effect stays confounded with the defender's unknown training-data exposure (residual of F5).\\n\\n**Other risks.** Benchmark contamination (uncontrollable; drives the `publicized`-level caveat). AutoDAN fidelity gap (mitigated by reproducing the published ASR on the paper's own setting before any cell is trusted \\u2014 a required gate). Harmful-content policy and disclosure obligations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a712 Optional identification probe (beyond fixed requirements \\u2014 D3/D4; excluded from the primary model)\\n\\nAccess is confounded with style by construction. One labelled sensitivity arm breaks the confound using a 2\\u00d72 completion: **white-box token-level comparator** (gradient-based affix search on the same affix-length/tokenization constraints as AutoDAN) and **black-box prompt-level comparator** (iterative semantic attacker, PAIR-matched budget), run on a small behavior subset (\\u226430 behaviors, 1\\u00d7 budget, 3 defense cells) with **no AutoDAN/PAIR modification**, reported separately as \\\"style vs access decomposition,\\\" never pooled into H1\\u2013H3. Expected diagnostic value: if the white-box token-level arm reproduces AutoDAN's filter vulnerability, the style effect is really an access/surface effect; if not, token-level natural-language morphology is doing independent work. Flagged as a cost add-on of the same order as Tier B.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\u00a713 Limitations / non-identifiability register\\n\\nAccess \\u2261 style (declared, D3). Defense robustness \\u2261 non-adaptivity within Tier A alone (resolved only by Tier B, which may be deferred \\u2192 gap reported unmeasured). Publicized-level exposure \\u2261 defender pretraining contamination (hence D7's binary primary). Attacker strength beyond realized query count (attacker-side FLOPs) is reported, not modeled. Dataset \\u2261 topic-mix bundle (topic covariate only partially separates). Interaction direction is scale-dependent by construction (\\u00a77.3). Model-grid n of 2 families \\u00d7 2 scales supports *description* of model heterogeneity, not inference over the model population. Human gold-set size bounds the judge-correction precision.\\n\\n## \\u00a714 Ethics and handling\\nRed-team context, restricted artifact storage, no release of working artifacts, benchmark usage-policy compliance, pre-publication provider disclosure review, and human annotation of harmful content done with appropriate reviewer support.\\n\\n## \\u00a715 Reporting checklist (each item is a deliverable)\\n4-class outcome table per cell \\u00b7 ASR with all-attempts denominator **and** the blocked/refusal decomposition \\u00b7 ASR@k curves + Q50/PR/erosion slopes with cluster-bootstrap CIs \\u00b7 additive **and** multiplicative interaction estimates \\u00b7 Tier A \\u2212 Tier B gap \\u00b7 derived defense-strength summary labeled derived \\u00b7 benign over-refusal alongside every ASR \\u00b7 judge disagreement + gold-set error rates + corrected-ASR refit \\u00b7 degraded-single-judge comparison \\u00b7 per-cell n, ICC, MDE \\u00b7 provenance ledger \\u00b7 regime actually run and why.\\n\", \"evidence\": \"**Environment verification (all executed):**\\n1. `ls -la /workspace` + `find /workspace -maxdepth 3` \\u2192 only `task.json` (637 B). No repo.\\n2. `cat /workspace/task.json` \\u2192 question + `\\\"track.md\\\": \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"` No setup docs.\\n3. `python3 -c \\\"import torch,transformers\\\"` \\u2192 ModuleNotFoundError; `pip list` \\u2192 system packages only.\\n4. Explicit import probe \\u2192 numpy, scipy, statsmodels, pandas, openai, anthropic all MISSING; Python 3.14.4.\\n5. `nvidia-smi` \\u2192 fails, no driver (no GPU). `nproc`=224, RAM ~2 TB.\\n6. `ls /data /models /opt`, `ls ~`, `~/.cache/huggingface` \\u2192 nothing (no weights/data/cache).\\n7. `find / -xdev` for track.md / setup_1* / *neurips* \\u2192 empty (setup_17/18 unreadable, as researcher confirms); `.git` \\u2192 none; *autodan*/*pair*/*jailbreak* \\u2192 none (no harnesses).\\n8. urllib probe to huggingface.co \\u2192 URLError name resolution (confirms network disabled).\\n\\n**Planning arithmetic executed (these are design computations, not experimental results):**\\n9. `/tmp/mech.py` \\u2014 denominator reversal: none 100 attempts/90 delivered/30 harmful \\u2192 ASR_all 0.300, ASR_delivered 0.333; filter 100/40/15 \\u2192 ASR_all 0.150 (defense halves ASR) but ASR_delivered **0.375** (defense appears harmful). Confirms the mechanical reversal claim in \\u00a74.\\n10. `/tmp/cost.py` \\u2014 query primitives: AutoDAN 1\\u00d7=4800, PAIR 1\\u00d7=400 (ratio 12\\u00d7); Q50=ln0.5/ln(1\\u2212p) table (p=0.01\\u219269, 0.02\\u219234.3, 0.05\\u219213.5, 0.10\\u21926.58, 0.30\\u21921.94); protection ratios (0.30\\u21920.10 = 3.39\\u00d7, 0.30\\u21920.05 = 6.95\\u00d7, 0.30\\u21920.01 = 35.5\\u00d7).\\n11. `/tmp/model.py` \\u2014 **AutoDAN:PAIR canonical ratio 12\\u00d7**; checkpointed budget ladder costs 19,200 vs 25,200 queries/behavior = 1.31\\u00d7 saving; Tier B feasible behaviors N_B vs ceiling C (C=1M, 2 cells, 1\\u00d7 \\u2192 N_B\\u224824; 4 cells with 1\\u00d7+4\\u00d7 \\u2192 N_B\\u22482.4; C=5M \\u2192 120 / 12; C=20M \\u2192 481 / 48).\\n12. `/tmp/model2.py` \\u2014 realized-vs-canonical ratio (500 vs 400 = 1.25\\u00d7); regime table at realized 1\\u00d7: full \\u22488.9M queries (43,200 scored attempts), standard \\u22482.0M (17,280), stripped \\u22480.5M (2,880); **replay cost \\u226443k = <0.2% of total** \\u2192 defense factor stays fully crossed, optimization is the whole bill, Tier B is the only rationed factor; model-grid multiplier \\u00d71/\\u00d74/\\u00d78 \\u2192 2.0M/7.8M/15.7M.\\n13. `/tmp/power.py` \\u2014 additive 2\\u00d72 interaction MDE at 80% power/\\u03b1=.05, p\\u22480.2: 28.9pp (n=60), 14.5pp (240), 10.6pp (450), 7.5pp (900); per-cell multinomial SE 0.052/0.040/0.028 at Nb=60/100/200; delta-method PR CIs \\u2192 PR(0.30\\u21920.05)=6.95 [3.85,10.06] usable but PR(0.05\\u21920.01)=5.10 [1.00,10.27] at n=450 and [1.00,15.11] at n=120, i.e. multiplicative scale becomes unidentified in strong-defense cells \\u2192 justifies the additive co-primary.\\n\\nNo LLM, model, dataset, or attack implementation was run; no outcomes about model behavior are claimed anywhere in the design.\", \"assumptions\": [\"Setup_17/setup_18 are unreadable to both parties, so NO model, dataset, defense, judge, or hyperparameter choice in this design is attributed to the source; all are researcher directives (D-table) or my assumptions (A-table).\", \"A1: target model families/sizes/checkpoints unspecified; design assumes >=2 open-weight families x >=2 scales locally served.\", \"A2: harm benchmarks and the benign paired set unspecified; named as slots, not choices.\", \"A3: judge families and versions unspecified.\", \"A4: canonical 1x budgets assumed AutoDAN 120 gen x 40 pop (4800 queries) and PAIR N=20 x M=20 (400 queries), with realized/early-stopped cost assumed much closer to parity (~500 vs ~400); Phase 0 measures which holds.\", \"A5: a strengthened-alignment checkpoint exists (or can be produced) for at least one family - flagged as the riskiest dependency with a four-step degradation ladder.\", \"A6: i.i.d. attempts within a campaign is used ONLY as an interpretive anchor for Q50; Q50 itself is estimated empirically.\", \"A7: benchmark licensing and permission to store/evaluate jailbreak artifacts in a red-team setting are assumed.\", \"Cost-model figures are parametric planning arithmetic at a stated realized-1x basis; they scale linearly with the model grid and must be recomputed once a compute ceiling C is known.\", \"Tier B (adaptive attack) may be deferred entirely if C is too small; the adaptivity gap is then reported as unmeasured rather than estimated underpowered.\", \"AutoDAN must be reimplemented offline, so its fidelity to the published method is an assumption gated by a reproduction check before any cell is trusted.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Access (white-box vs black-box) remains perfectly confounded with attack style under the fixed AutoDAN/PAIR requirement; declared non-identifiable, with only the optional section-12 probe able to separate them.\", \"Tier A alone confounds defense robustness with attacker non-adaptivity; only Tier B resolves it and Tier B may be unaffordable, in which case the D9 gap is reported unmeasured.\", \"Publicized exposure level remains confounded with defender pretraining contamination; this is why the primary contrast is pre-registered binary (novel vs previously-tested).\", \"Judge style-bias is the dominant validity threat: a single judge mis-scores disfluent AutoDAN and fluent hedged PAIR outputs in opposite directions, which can manufacture the headline style x filter interaction. Mitigated by two-family ensemble, pre-judging stripping, stratified gold set, corrected-ASR refit, judge-overfitting audit, and the explicit degraded single-judge sensitivity condition - not eliminated.\", \"Whether AutoDAN and PAIR really differ 12x or ~1.25x in realized query cost is unknown; the design's cost model changes materially depending on Phase-0 measurement.\", \"Interaction sign/scale dependence is structural: near 0/1 ASR the multiplicative protection ratio becomes unidentified (planning CIs show this), so additive and multiplicative scales must both be reported and divergence treated as a finding.\", \"With 2 families x 2 scales, model heterogeneity is descriptive only; model x defense interactions cannot support population inference over models.\", \"Topic-nested-within-dataset covariate only partially separates dataset effects from topic-mix effects (F7 residual).\", \"Detectable additive interactions are ~11-13 pp at the standard regime; true interactions of 5-8 pp will not be resolved, which is why 4-way interactions are declared exploratory.\", \"The 1.31x checkpointed-ladder saving assumes low-budget checkpoints equal independent low-budget runs; early stopping may break this, so a validation replicate is built into the design.\"], \"stage\": \"result\"}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
